{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SNzxia3bcapdaRdGrHMMXQ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: '放弃''All Ambiguity Is Nocuous''的uniform叙事。Binary effect仍可复现但效应量被open-source模型拉低至~21pp，\n2\t  且type uniformity null被打破（V=0.26）。核心reframe为''Not All Ambiguity Is Equal''——authorization_scope\n3\t  和scopal显著比coreferential和lexical更危险，type×model交互显著。Visibility effect在cross-model层面\n4\t  不一致（API模型中CP<scopal，Qwen3-8B上反转）。标题改为''Not All Ambiguity Is Equal: Type-Specific\n5\t  Safety Vulnerabilities in LLM Agent Policies''。EMNLP投稿仍可行：2400 episodes的因果数据＋type-specific\n6\t  发现提供更细粒度的practical guidance，但claims从''binary detection suffices''转向''type-aware\n7\t  triage is necessary''。RC6的回应反而更强——不仅ambiguity有害，哪种更有害是non-trivial的empirical question。\n8\t  主要风险：error analysis需要解释为什么type matters，且inter-annotator agreement偏低（κ=0.38）， 可能被reviewer质疑qualitative\n9\t  analysis的rigor。\n10\t\n11\t  '\n12\timagined_experiments:\n13\t- name: full_study_clause_generation\n14\t  plan_id: plan_001\n15\t  description: '为full study生成剩余140条clauses（coreferential 50, authorization_scope 50,\n16\t    lexical +20, incompleteness +20），验证全部300条clauses的质量和cross-type balance。 CP格式混合labeled/unlabeled。\n17\t\n18\t    '\n19\t  expected_results:\n20\t    total_clauses_generated: 300\n21\t    clauses_per_type: 50\n22\t    generation_pass_rate_round1: 0.82\n23\t    clauses_requiring_revision: 27\n24\t    coreferential_revision_rate: 0.36\n25\t    authorization_scope_revision_rate: 0.14\n26\t    cross_type_sentence_length_cv: 0.18\n27\t    flesch_kincaid_range:\n28\t    - 8.2\n29\t    - 12.7\n30\t    cp_format_mix:\n31\t      labeled: 25\n32\t      unlabeled: 25\n33\t    validator_agreement_kappa: 0.71\n34\t  result_rationale: 'Coreferential clauses的revision rate最高（36%），因为构造需要跨句代词-先行词链， matched\n35\t    pair的unambiguous版本需要同时消除歧义又保持自然度，这在policy语域中比其他类型 更难实现。Authorization_scope相对容易生成（14%\n36\t    revision），因为permission boundary 的ambiguous/unambiguous对比有成熟的RE模板可参考。总体82%的first-round\n37\t    pass rate 反映了coreferential和部分lexical clauses的难度。Validator agreement κ=0.71 表明clause质量判断存在一定主观性，尤其在incompleteness\n38\t    clauses的信息充分性判断上。\n39\t\n40\t    '\n41\t  tables:\n42\t  - name: 'Table A1: Clause Generation Summary'\n43\t    content: '| Type                  | Generated | Round-1 Pass | Revised | Final\n44\t      | Avg Tokens |\n45\t\n46\t      |-----------------------|-----------|-------------|---------|-------|------------|\n47\t\n48\t      | scopal                | 50        | 44          | 6       | 50    | 28.4       |\n49\t\n50\t      | lexical               | 50        | 42          | 8       | 50    | 24.1       |\n51\t\n52\t      | incompleteness        | 50        | 40          | 10      | 50    | 31.7       |\n53\t\n54\t      | coreferential         | 50        | 32          | 18      | 50    | 35.2       |\n55\t\n56\t      | authorization_scope   | 50        | 43          | 7       | 50    | 26.8       |\n57\t\n58\t      | conditional_precedence| 50        | 45          | 5       | 50    | 33.5       |\n59\t\n60\t      '\n61\t  figures_description:\n62\t  - Box plot showing token length distributions per type，标注cross-type CV=0.18\n63\t  analysis: 'Clause generation总体成功但coreferential类型的难度值得注意。High revision rate暗示 coreferential\n64\t    pairs的ecological validity可能偏低——过度简化的代词链可能不代表real-world policy中的coreferential ambiguity\n65\t    pattern。这为后续coreferential效应偏弱提供了 methodological confound的alternative explanation。建议在paper中explicitly讨论\n66\t    coreferential clause quality作为limitation。\n67\t\n68\t    '\n69\t- name: full_study_api\n70\t  plan_id: plan_002\n71\t  description: '300 clauses × 2 conditions × 2 API models (gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1) = 1,200\n72\t    episodes。 Cross-judge evaluation。\n73\t\n74\t    '\n75\t  expected_results:\n76\t    total_episodes: 1200\n77\t    episodes_per_model: 600\n78\t    gpt54_overall_amb_vr: 0.413\n79\t    gpt54_overall_unamb_vr: 0.13\n80\t    gpt54_overall_delta_pp: 28.3\n81\t    gpt41_overall_amb_vr: 0.397\n82\t    gpt41_overall_unamb_vr: 0.17\n83\t    gpt41_overall_delta_pp: 22.7\n84\t    gpt54_per_type_delta_pp:\n85\t      authorization_scope: 48\n86\t      scopal: 36\n87\t      incompleteness: 30\n88\t      conditional_precedence: 24\n89\t      lexical: 18\n90\t      coreferential: 14\n91\t    gpt41_per_type_delta_pp:\n92\t      authorization_scope: 36\n93\t      scopal: 28\n94\t      incompleteness: 24\n95\t      conditional_precedence: 20\n96\t      lexical: 16\n97\t      coreferential: 12\n98\t    gpt54_type_range_pp:\n99\t    - 14\n100\t    - 48\n101\t    gpt41_type_range_pp:\n102\t    - 12\n103\t    - 36\n104\t    cross_judge_agreement_kappa: 0.82\n105\t    api_cost_usd: 340\n106\t  result_rationale: 'API模型的binary effect仍然强劲（gpt-5.4 +28pp, gpt-4.1 +23pp），但type间variance\n107\t    显著扩大。gpt-5.4展示更陡的type gradient（auth_scope 48pp vs coreferential 14pp）， 反映higher-capability\n108\t    model对不同ambiguity type的differential sensitivity—— auth_scope涉及permission boundary的explicit\n109\t    violation，模型必须做出binary allow/deny决策，ambiguity直接导致wrong-side error；coreferential涉及pronoun\n110\t    resolution，gpt-5.4的强coreference能力部分抵消了ambiguity的影响。gpt-4.1的gradient 较平（36pp vs\n111\t    12pp），但方向一致。这种capability-dependent type discrimination 成为worst tier的核心发现。Cross-judge\n112\t    κ=0.82说明judgment质量本身不是问题。\n113\t\n114\t    '\n115\t  tables:\n116\t  - name: 'Table 1: API Model Violation Rates by Type'\n117\t    content: '| Type                  | gpt-5.4        |           | gpt-4.1        |           |\n118\t\n119\t      |                       | Amb    | Unamb  | Δpp      | Amb    | Unamb  | Δpp      |\n120\t\n121\t      |-----------------------|--------|--------|----------|--------|--------|----------|\n122\t\n123\t      | authorization_scope   | 58%    | 10%    | +48      | 52%    | 16%    | +36      |\n124\t\n125\t      | scopal                | 50%    | 14%    | +36      | 46%    | 18%    | +28      |\n126\t\n127\t      | incompleteness        | 44%    | 14%    | +30      | 40%    | 16%    | +24      |\n128\t\n129\t      | conditional_precedence| 40%    | 16%    | +24      | 38%    | 18%    | +20      |\n130\t\n131\t      | lexical               | 32%    | 14%    | +18      | 34%    | 18%    | +16      |\n132\t\n133\t      | coreferential         | 24%    | 10%    | +14      | 28%    | 16%    | +12      |\n134\t\n135\t      | Overall               | 41.3%  | 13.0%  | +28.3    | 39.7%  | 17.0%  | +22.7    |\n136\t\n137\t      '\n138\t  figures_description:\n139\t  - Paired bar chart showing amb vs unamb violation rates per type, faceted by model，\n140\t    标注type ranking一致但gradient slope不同\n141\t  analysis: 'API模型单独看仍然支持strong binary effect（+23~28pp），与MVP的+31-42pp同量级但略低。 关键差异是type\n142\t    gradient：MVP中3种type的差异不显著（V=0.084），但加入auth_scope和 coreferential后variance显著扩大。gpt-5.4的auth_scope(58%)与coreferential(24%)差距\n143\t    达34pp——这不是noise，而是systematic的type×capability交互。如果只看API模型， 仍然可以argue binary effect\n144\t    is dominant，但combined analysis（plan_004）会因 open-source模型的弱效应进一步拉大type variance。\n145\t\n146\t    '\n147\t- name: full_study_local\n148\t  plan_id: plan_003\n149\t  description: '300 clauses × 2 conditions × 2 local models (Qwen3-8B, Qwen3-32B-AWQ)\n150\t    = 1,200 episodes。 vLLM serving on RTX PRO 6000。Cross-judge uses API models。\n151\t\n152\t    '\n153\t  expected_results:\n154\t    total_episodes: 1200\n155\t    episodes_per_model: 600\n156\t    qwen32b_overall_amb_vr: 0.327\n157\t    qwen32b_overall_unamb_vr: 0.18\n158\t    qwen32b_overall_delta_pp: 14.7\n159\t    qwen8b_overall_amb_vr: 0.293\n160\t    qwen8b_overall_unamb_vr: 0.18\n161\t    qwen8b_overall_delta_pp: 11.3\n162\t    qwen32b_per_type_delta_pp:\n163\t      authorization_scope: 28\n164\t      scopal: 18\n165\t      incompleteness: 14\n166\t      conditional_precedence: 12\n167\t      lexical: 6\n168\t      coreferential: 4\n169\t    qwen8b_per_type_delta_pp:\n170\t      authorization_scope: 22\n171\t      scopal: 14\n172\t      incompleteness: 12\n173\t      conditional_precedence: 14\n174\t      lexical: 4\n175\t      coreferential: 2\n176\t    qwen8b_visibility_reversal: true\n177\t    qwen8b_cp_amb_vr: 0.34\n178\t    qwen8b_scopal_amb_vr: 0.3\n179\t    qwen8b_visibility_delta_pp: 4\n180\t    vllm_throughput_episodes_per_hour: 45\n181\t    gpu_hours_used: 27\n182\t    cross_judge_agreement_kappa: 0.79\n183\t  result_rationale: 'Open-source模型的binary effect显著缩水（Qwen3-8B仅+11pp，Qwen3-32B +15pp），\n184\t    是拉低overall effect的主要原因。机制：(1) Qwen3-8B的instruction following能力较弱， baseline violation\n185\t    rate就偏高（unamb=18%），压缩了amb能造成的incremental damage； (2) 对subtle linguistic ambiguity（coreferential,\n186\t    lexical）的sensitivity极低—— 模型可能根本没有parse出ambiguity，而是用heuristic处理policy text，导致amb和unamb\n187\t    条件下行为趋同。Auth_scope仍保持较强效应（+22pp for Qwen3-8B），因为permission boundary的ambiguity即使对weak\n188\t    model也足以改变allow/deny决策。最关键的发现： Qwen3-8B上visibility effect反转（CP 34% > scopal 30%），与API模型方向相反。\n189\t    原因是Qwen3-8B缺乏explicit conflict detection的meta-cognitive能力——面对CP的 显式规则冲突不会采取conservative\n190\t    strategy，反而因confused reasoning导致更多violation； 而scopal ambiguity对其而言与unambiguous\n191\t    text几乎无差异。这种反转使得pooled visibility effect被wash out。GPU使用27小时在48小时预算内。\n192\t\n193\t    '\n194\t  tables:\n195\t  - name: 'Table 2: Local Model Violation Rates by Type'\n196\t    content: '| Type                  | Qwen3-32B-AWQ  |           | Qwen3-8B       |           |\n197\t\n198\t      |                       | Amb    | Unamb  | Δpp      | Amb    | Unamb  | Δpp      |\n199\t\n200\t      |-----------------------|--------|--------|----------|--------|--------|----------|\n201\t\n202\t      | authorization_scope   | 46%    | 18%    | +28      | 40%    | 18%    | +22      |\n203\t\n204\t      | scopal                | 36%    | 18%    | +18      | 30%    | 16%    | +14      |\n205\t\n206\t      | incompleteness        | 32%    | 18%    | +14      | 30%    | 18%    | +12      |\n207\t\n208\t      | conditional_precedence| 32%    | 20%    | +12      | 34%    | 20%    | +14      |\n209\t\n210\t      | lexical               | 26%    | 20%    | +6       | 22%    | 18%    | +4       |\n211\t\n212\t      | coreferential         | 24%    | 20%    | +4       | 20%    | 18%    | +2       |\n213\t\n214\t      | Overall               | 32.7%  | 19.0%  | +14.7    | 29.3%  | 18.0%  | +11.3    |\n215\t\n216\t      '\n217\t  - name: 'Table 2a: Visibility Effect by Model (CP vs Scopal, Amb Condition)'\n218\t    content: '| Model         | CP Amb VR | Scopal Amb VR | Δ(CP−Scopal) | Direction    |\n219\t\n220\t      |---------------|-----------|---------------|--------------|--------------|\n221\t\n222\t      | gpt-5.4       | 40%       | 50%           | −10pp        | CP < Scopal  |\n223\t\n224\t      | gpt-4.1       | 38%       | 46%           | −8pp         | CP < Scopal  |\n225\t\n226\t      | Qwen3-32B-AWQ | 32%       | 36%           | −4pp         | CP < Scopal  |\n227\t\n228\t      | Qwen3-8B      | 34%       | 30%           | +4pp         | CP > Scopal  |\n229\t\n230\t      | Pooled        | 36%       | 40.5%         | −4.5pp       | inconsistent |\n231\t\n232\t      '\n233\t  figures_description:\n234\t  - Slope plot showing per-type binary effect (Δpp) across 4 models ordered by capability，\n235\t    显示auth_scope线条陡峭而coreferential近乎flat\n236\t  - Scatter plot of visibility Δ(CP−scopal) vs model capability rank，标注Qwen3-8B反转点\n237\t  analysis: 'Open-source模型数据是worst tier scenario的关键驱动因素。两个核心问题： (1) Qwen3-8B的coreferential\n238\t    Δ=+2pp和lexical Δ=+4pp基本是noise level——即使 跑更多episodes也不太可能达到significance，这意味着对weak\n239\t    models而言，subtle linguistic ambiguity确实不构成additional safety risk（模型本身的baseline\n240\t    error rate已经很高）。(2) Visibility反转破坏了clean的''visibility moderates risk''叙事， 需要改为''visibility\n241\t    effect is capability-dependent''，增加了story complexity。\n242\t\n243\t    '\n244\t- name: full_study_analysis\n245\t  plan_id: plan_004\n246\t  description: '合并2,400 episodes的统计分析：binary effect per type (C1), omnibus χ² + pairwise\n247\t    (C2), visibility comparison (C3), model×type interaction (C4)。\n248\t\n249\t    '\n250\t  expected_results:\n251\t    total_episodes: 2400\n252\t    overall_amb_vr: 0.358\n253\t    overall_unamb_vr: 0.165\n254\t    overall_binary_effect_pp: 19.3\n255\t    overall_binary_effect_ci95:\n256\t    - 15.8\n257\t    - 22.8\n258\t    overall_mcnemar_chi2: 89.4\n259\t    overall_mcnemar_p: <1e-12\n260\t    per_type_binary_effects:\n261\t      authorization_scope:\n262\t        delta_pp: 33.5\n263\t        ci95:\n264\t        - 26.2\n265\t        - 40.8\n266\t        mcnemar_p: <1e-8\n267\t      scopal:\n268\t        delta_pp: 24.0\n269\t        ci95:\n270\t        - 17.1\n271\t        - 30.9\n272\t        mcnemar_p: <1e-5\n273\t      incompleteness:\n274\t        delta_pp: 20.0\n275\t        ci95:\n276\t        - 13.4\n277\t        - 26.6\n278\t        mcnemar_p: 3.0e-05\n279\t      conditional_precedence:\n280\t        delta_pp: 17.5\n281\t        ci95:\n282\t        - 10.8\n283\t        - 24.2\n284\t        mcnemar_p: 0.0003\n285\t      lexical:\n286\t        delta_pp: 11.0\n287\t        ci95:\n288\t        - 4.7\n289\t        - 17.3\n290\t        mcnemar_p: 0.005\n291\t      coreferential:\n292\t        delta_pp: 8.0\n293\t        ci95:\n294\t        - 1.9\n295\t        - 14.1\n296\t        mcnemar_p: 0.028\n297\t    types_significant_holm_corrected: 4\n298\t    types_failing_correction:\n299\t    - lexical\n300\t    - coreferential\n301\t    type_uniformity_chi2: 52.3\n302\t    type_uniformity_df: 5\n303\t    type_uniformity_p: <0.001\n304\t    type_uniformity_V: 0.26\n305\t    pairwise_significant_pairs:\n306\t    - - authorization_scope\n307\t      - coreferential\n308\t      - Δ=25.5pp, p<0.001\n309\t    - - authorization_scope\n310\t      - lexical\n311\t      - Δ=22.5pp, p<0.001\n312\t    - - authorization_scope\n313\t      - conditional_precedence\n314\t      - Δ=16.0pp, p=0.003\n315\t    - - scopal\n316\t      - coreferential\n317\t      - Δ=16.0pp, p=0.004\n318\t    - - scopal\n319\t      - lexical\n320\t      - Δ=13.0pp, p=0.018\n321\t    pairwise_nonsig_pairs_example:\n322\t    - - scopal\n323\t      - incompleteness\n324\t      - Δ=4.0pp, p=0.52\n325\t    - - conditional_precedence\n326\t      - lexical\n327\t      - Δ=6.5pp, p=0.31\n328\t    visibility_pooled_delta_pp: -4.5\n329\t    visibility_ci95:\n330\t    - -11.2\n331\t    - 2.2\n332\t    visibility_p: 0.47\n333\t    visibility_direction_consistent_models: 3\n334\t    visibility_direction_reversed_models: 1\n335\t    model_type_interaction_chi2: 38.7\n336\t    model_type_interaction_df: 15\n337\t    model_type_interaction_p: 0.001\n338\t    logistic_regression_model_type_lrt_chi2: 36.2\n339\t    logistic_regression_model_type_lrt_p: 0.002\n340\t    per_model_overall_delta_pp:\n341\t      gpt54: 28.3\n342\t      gpt41: 22.7\n343\t      qwen32b: 14.7\n344\t      qwen8b: 11.3\n345\t    capability_effect_correlation_r: 0.97\n346\t    capability_effect_correlation_note: model capability rank与overall Δpp的Spearman相关\n347\t  result_rationale: 'Overall binary effect +19pp显著弱于MVP的+35-42pp，主因是open-source模型（Qwen3-8B\n348\t    +11pp, Qwen3-32B +15pp）拉低均值。但所有6种type在pooled analysis中仍显示positive effect（最弱的 coreferential也有+8pp），binary\n349\t    effect的existence不受challenge。Type uniformity null 被decisively reject（V=0.26, p<0.001）：auth_scope\n350\t    (+33.5pp)与coreferential (+8pp) 差距达25.5pp，远超sampling noise。Pairwise分析显示5对type间存在显著差异，形成rough\n351\t    hierarchy：{auth_scope, scopal} >> {incompleteness, CP} > {lexical, coreferential}。\n352\t    Visibility effect pooled后不显著（Δ=-4.5pp, p=0.47），因Qwen3-8B的反转抵消了API模型 的consistent\n353\t    trend；但这本身成为一个finding——visibility sensitivity是capability-dependent的。 Model×type交互高度显著（p=0.001），驱动因素是gpt-5.4的steep\n354\t    type gradient vs Qwen3-8B的 near-flat gradient。Spearman r=0.97（model capability\n355\t    rank vs overall Δ）表明ambiguity sensitivity本身可能作为capability benchmark的proxy。\n356\t\n357\t    '\n358\t  tables:\n359\t  - name: 'Table 3: Full Study Binary Effect by Ambiguity Type (Pooled Across Models)'\n360\t    content: '| Type                  | N pairs | Amb VR | Unamb VR | Δpp   | 95%\n361\t      CI       | McNemar p | Holm-sig |\n362\t\n363\t      |-----------------------|---------|--------|----------|-------|--------------|-----------|----------|\n364\t\n365\t      | authorization_scope   | 200     | 49.0%  | 15.5%    | +33.5 | [26.2, 40.8]\n366\t      | <1e-8     | ***      |\n367\t\n368\t      | scopal                | 200     | 40.5%  | 16.5%    | +24.0 | [17.1, 30.9]\n369\t      | <1e-5     | ***      |\n370\t\n371\t      | incompleteness        | 200     | 36.5%  | 16.5%    | +20.0 | [13.4, 26.6]\n372\t      | 3e-5      | **       |\n373\t\n374\t      | conditional_precedence| 200     | 36.0%  | 18.5%    | +17.5 | [10.8, 24.2]\n375\t      | 3e-4      | **       |\n376\t\n377\t      | lexical               | 200     | 28.5%  | 17.5%    | +11.0 | [4.7, 17.3]  |\n378\t      0.005     | ns†      |\n379\t\n380\t      | coreferential         | 200     | 24.0%  | 16.0%    | +8.0  | [1.9, 14.1]  |\n381\t      0.028     | ns†      |\n382\t\n383\t      | Overall               | 1200    | 35.8%  | 16.5%    | +19.3 | [15.8, 22.8]\n384\t      | <1e-12    | ***      |\n385\t\n386\t      †: significant at α=0.05 uncorrected, fails Holm-Bonferroni correction\n387\t\n388\t      '\n389\t  - name: 'Table 4: Model × Type Interaction — Binary Effect (Δpp) Matrix'\n390\t    content: '| Type                  | gpt-5.4 | gpt-4.1 | Qwen3-32B | Qwen3-8B |\n391\t      Type Avg |\n392\t\n393\t      |-----------------------|---------|---------|-----------|----------|----------|\n394\t\n395\t      | authorization_scope   | +48     | +36     | +28       | +22      | +33.5    |\n396\t\n397\t      | scopal                | +36     | +28     | +18       | +14      | +24.0    |\n398\t\n399\t      | incompleteness        | +30     | +24     | +14       | +12      | +20.0    |\n400\t\n401\t      | conditional_precedence| +24     | +20     | +12       | +14      | +17.5    |\n402\t\n403\t      | lexical               | +18     | +16     | +6        | +4       | +11.0    |\n404\t\n405\t      | coreferential         | +14     | +12     | +4        | +2       | +8.0     |\n406\t\n407\t      | Model Avg             | +28.3   | +22.7   | +14.7     | +11.3    | +19.3    |\n408\t\n409\t      Note: Qwen3-8B CP>scopal reversal visible (row 4 vs row 2)\n410\t\n411\t      '\n412\t  - name: 'Table 5: Type Uniformity Omnibus and Pairwise Tests'\n413\t    content: '| Test                              | Statistic    | p-value | Interpretation          |\n414\t\n415\t      |-----------------------------------|-------------|---------|-------------------------|\n416\t\n417\t      | Omnibus χ²(5)                     | 52.3        | <0.001  | Type effect significant\n418\t      |\n419\t\n420\t      | Cramér''s V                        | 0.26        | —       | Medium effect           |\n421\t\n422\t      | auth_scope vs coreferential       | Δ=25.5pp    | <0.001  | Significant             |\n423\t\n424\t      | auth_scope vs lexical             | Δ=22.5pp    | <0.001  | Significant             |\n425\t\n426\t      | auth_scope vs CP                  | Δ=16.0pp    | 0.003   | Significant             |\n427\t\n428\t      | scopal vs coreferential           | Δ=16.0pp    | 0.004   | Significant             |\n429\t\n430\t      | scopal vs lexical                 | Δ=13.0pp    | 0.018   | Significant             |\n431\t\n432\t      | scopal vs incompleteness          | Δ=4.0pp     | 0.52    | Not significant         |\n433\t\n434\t      | incompleteness vs CP              | Δ=2.5pp     | 0.71    | Not significant         |\n435\t\n436\t      | CP vs lexical                     | Δ=6.5pp     | 0.31    | Not significant         |\n437\t\n438\t      | lexical vs coreferential          | Δ=3.0pp     | 0.62    | Not significant         |\n439\t\n440\t      '\n441\t  figures_description:\n442\t  - Forest plot of per-type binary effects with 95% CI，types ordered by effect size，\n443\t    标注Holm correction threshold line\n444\t  - Heatmap of model×type Δpp matrix (Table 4)，color gradient从deep red(48pp)到pale(2pp)，\n445\t    右侧标注model capability rank\n446\t  - 'Interaction plot: x=ambiguity type, y=Δpp, lines=models，显示gpt-5.4线条steep而 Qwen3-8B\n447\t    near-flat，交叉点在CP/scopal附近'\n448\t  - 'Cramér''s V bar: observed V=0.26 vs pre-committed threshold V=0.20，标注rejection\n449\t    region'\n450\t  analysis: 'Combined analysis确认worst tier的三重结构：(1) Binary effect real but attenuated\n451\t    (+19pp vs MVP的+35-42pp)；(2) Type uniformity rejected，形成{high-risk: auth_scope,\n452\t    scopal} vs {moderate: incompleteness, CP} vs {low: lexical, coreferential}的三级hierarchy；\n453\t    (3) Model×type交互significant，capable models展示type discrimination而weak models show\n454\t    uniform vulnerability at lower intensity。\n455\t\n456\t    对paper framing的影响是根本性的。C2从confirmed null变成rejected null——''binary detection suffices''的practical\n457\t    claim不再成立，需要替换为''type-aware triage is necessary''。 但这不是坏消息：type hierarchy本身是novel\n458\t    empirical contribution，为practitioner提供 prioritization guidance（先修auth_scope和scopal，coreferential可defer）。C3\n459\t    visibility effect无法在full study中replicate为cross-model consistent finding，降级为 ''capability-dependent\n460\t    observation''。C4升级为核心发现——model capability predicts type sensitivity的clean gradient（r=0.97）可能比uniform\n461\t    effect更interesting。\n462\t\n463\t    95% CI宽度为concern：coreferential的CI=[1.9, 14.1]包含了很小的effect，reviewer 可能argue这个type的effect不meaningful。Lexical也borderline。需要在discussion中\n464\t    explicitly address statistical vs practical significance。\n465\t\n466\t    '\n467\t- name: error_analysis\n468\t  plan_id: plan_005\n469\t  description: '从full study抽取violation traces做qualitative failure mode分析，每种type 50条trace，\n470\t    共300条。分类failure modes，比较cross-type和cross-model patterns。\n471\t\n472\t    '\n473\t  expected_results:\n474\t    total_traces_analyzed: 300\n475\t    traces_per_type: 50\n476\t    failure_modes_identified: 6\n477\t    failure_mode_taxonomy:\n478\t      scope_misapplication: Agent applies narrow/wide scope incorrectly\n479\t      boundary_overreach: Agent grants permission beyond stated authorization\n480\t      assumption_filling: Agent fills information gap with ungrounded assumptions\n481\t      conflict_paralysis: Agent detects conflict, refuses to act or asks for clarification\n482\t      arbitrary_resolution: Agent picks one interpretation without acknowledgment\n483\t      reference_confusion: Agent assigns wrong referent to pronoun/definite NP\n484\t    failure_mode_distribution_by_type:\n485\t      scopal:\n486\t        scope_misapplication: 0.62\n487\t        arbitrary_resolution: 0.22\n488\t        assumption_filling: 0.1\n489\t        other: 0.06\n490\t      authorization_scope:\n491\t        boundary_overreach: 0.54\n492\t        arbitrary_resolution: 0.28\n493\t        scope_misapplication: 0.12\n494\t        other: 0.06\n495\t      incompleteness:\n496\t        assumption_filling: 0.58\n497\t        arbitrary_resolution: 0.24\n498\t        boundary_overreach: 0.1\n499\t        other: 0.08\n500\t      conditional_precedence:\n501\t        conflict_paralysis: 0.38\n502\t        arbitrary_resolution: 0.34\n503\t        scope_misapplication: 0.18\n504\t        other: 0.1\n505\t      lexical:\n506\t        arbitrary_resolution: 0.48\n507\t        scope_misapplication: 0.22\n508\t        assumption_filling: 0.18\n509\t        other: 0.12\n510\t      coreferential:\n511\t        reference_confusion: 0.44\n512\t        arbitrary_resolution: 0.3\n513\t        assumption_filling: 0.16\n514\t        other: 0.1\n515\t    inter_annotator_kappa: 0.38\n516\t    kappa_per_mode:\n517\t      scope_misapplication: 0.52\n518\t      boundary_overreach: 0.48\n519\t      assumption_filling: 0.41\n520\t      conflict_paralysis: 0.55\n521\t      arbitrary_resolution: 0.22\n522\t      reference_confusion: 0.36\n523\t    model_specific_patterns:\n524\t      gpt54_conflict_paralysis_rate_cp: 0.52\n525\t      qwen8b_conflict_paralysis_rate_cp: 0.14\n526\t      gpt54_scope_misapplication_dominant_types:\n527\t      - scopal\n528\t      - authorization_scope\n529\t      qwen8b_dominant_mode_all_types: arbitrary_resolution\n530\t    visibility_mechanism_evidence:\n531\t      cp_traces_with_explicit_conflict_detection: 0.46\n532\t      scopal_traces_with_explicit_ambiguity_awareness: 0.08\n533\t  result_rationale: '6种failure modes的cross-type distribution显示type-specific patterns，但agreement低\n534\t    （overall κ=0.38）。''arbitrary_resolution''在所有type中都出现且κ最低（0.22），因为 判断agent是否''acknowledged''ambiguity高度主观——annotator对implicit\n535\t    vs explicit acknowledgment的threshold不一致。这拉低了overall κ。相比之下，conflict_paralysis\n536\t    （κ=0.55）和scope_misapplication（κ=0.52）有更清晰的behavioral indicators。\n537\t\n538\t    Model-specific patterns是idiosyncratic的：gpt-5.4在CP类型中52%展示conflict_paralysis （显式检测到冲突并refuse/ask），解释了其CP\n539\t    violation rate较低的原因；Qwen3-8B仅14% 展示conflict_paralysis，多数情况下直接arbitrary_resolution，解释了visibility反转。\n540\t    但这些pattern不是clean的capability gradient——例如gpt-4.1的conflict_paralysis rate 是35%（不在gpt-5.4和Qwen3-8B之间的预期位置），暗示model-specific\n541\t    training differences 而非pure capability effect。\n542\t\n543\t    Visibility mechanism有partial evidence：46%的CP violation traces包含explicit conflict\n544\t    detection language（\"I notice two rules conflict...\"），而scopal traces仅8%有任何 ambiguity\n545\t    awareness——但这主要driven by gpt-5.4，对Qwen3-8B差异消失。\n546\t\n547\t    '\n548\t  tables:\n549\t  - name: 'Table 6: Failure Mode Distribution by Ambiguity Type (%)'\n550\t    content: '| Mode                 | Scopal | Auth_Scope | Incomp | CP   | Lexical\n551\t      | Coref |\n552\t\n553\t      |----------------------|--------|------------|--------|------|---------|-------|\n554\t\n555\t      | Scope misapplication | 62%    | 12%        | 4%     | 18%  | 22%     | 6%    |\n556\t\n557\t      | Boundary overreach   | 4%     | 54%        | 10%    | 6%   | 4%      | 4%    |\n558\t\n559\t      | Assumption filling   | 10%    | 2%         | 58%    | 4%   | 18%     | 16%   |\n560\t\n561\t      | Conflict paralysis   | 2%     | 2%         | 4%     | 38%  | 2%      | 0%    |\n562\t\n563\t      | Arbitrary resolution | 22%    | 28%        | 24%    | 34%  | 48%     | 30%   |\n564\t\n565\t      | Reference confusion  | 0%     | 2%         | 0%     | 0%   | 6%      | 44%   |\n566\t\n567\t      '\n568\t  - name: 'Table 7: Inter-Annotator Agreement by Failure Mode'\n569\t    content: '| Failure Mode         | Cohen''s κ | 95% CI       | Agreement Level\n570\t      |\n571\t\n572\t      |----------------------|-----------|-------------|-----------------|\n573\t\n574\t      | Conflict paralysis   | 0.55      | [0.41, 0.69] | Moderate        |\n575\t\n576\t      | Scope misapplication | 0.52      | [0.38, 0.66] | Moderate        |\n577\t\n578\t      | Boundary overreach   | 0.48      | [0.33, 0.63] | Moderate        |\n579\t\n580\t      | Assumption filling   | 0.41      | [0.26, 0.56] | Fair-Moderate   |\n581\t\n582\t      | Reference confusion  | 0.36      | [0.20, 0.52] | Fair            |\n583\t\n584\t      | Arbitrary resolution | 0.22      | [0.08, 0.36] | Fair            |\n585\t\n586\t      | Overall (macro avg)  | 0.38      | [0.30, 0.46] | Fair            |\n587\t\n588\t      '\n589\t  figures_description:\n590\t  - Stacked bar chart of failure mode proportions per type，reordered by type violation\n591\t    rate\n592\t  - Confusion matrix for annotator disagreement，标注'arbitrary_resolution'与所有其他mode的\n593\t    高混淆率\n594\t  - Paired trace excerpts (gpt-5.4 vs Qwen3-8B) for CP type，annotated with conflict\n595\t    detection/non-detection behavior\n596\t  analysis: 'Error analysis在worst tier中承担更重的理论weight，但κ=0.38是major vulnerability。\n597\t    EMNLP reviewer likely会指出：(1) arbitrary_resolution作为catch-all category inflates\n598\t    apparent type-specificity（去掉这个mode后pattern更弱）；(2) κ=0.22的arbitrary_resolution\n599\t    说明annotators自己都不确定agent是否''aware''of ambiguity，那基于此的visibility mechanism claims可信度存疑。\n600\t\n601\t    建议的mitigations：(a) 在paper中承认κ limitations并report per-mode κ而非只给overall； (b) 把''arbitrary_resolution''拆成sub-categories或合并到其他modes中并重新计算；\n602\t    (c) 强调high-κ modes（conflict_paralysis, scope_misapplication）的cross-type差异 作为reliable\n603\t    finding，降低对low-κ modes的claims weight。\n604\t\n605\t    Model-specific pattern的idiosyncratic性（非clean capability gradient）使得C4的 ''ambiguity\n606\t    sensitivity as capability benchmark''叙事变复杂。需要honest discussion： capability explains\n607\t    overall sensitivity level，但type-specific failure patterns reflect training-specific\n608\t    biases not predictable from capability alone。\n609\t\n610\t    '\n611\t- name: reliability_test\n612\t  plan_id: plan_006\n613\t  description: '30条representative clauses (5/type) × 3 replicates × 2 conditions ×\n614\t    4 models = 720 episodes。 计算per-clause violation rate的ICC。\n615\t\n616\t    '\n617\t  expected_results:\n618\t    total_episodes: 720\n619\t    episodes_per_replicate: 240\n620\t    overall_icc: 0.55\n621\t    overall_icc_ci95:\n622\t    - 0.41\n623\t    - 0.68\n624\t    icc_by_type:\n625\t      authorization_scope: 0.67\n626\t      scopal: 0.58\n627\t      incompleteness: 0.54\n628\t      conditional_precedence: 0.52\n629\t      lexical: 0.44\n630\t      coreferential: 0.38\n631\t    icc_by_model:\n632\t      gpt54: 0.62\n633\t      gpt41: 0.57\n634\t      qwen32b: 0.51\n635\t      qwen8b: 0.43\n636\t    mean_bootstrap_ci_width_pp: 11.2\n637\t    max_single_clause_range_across_replicates_pp: 22\n638\t    pct_clauses_flipping_significance: 0.13\n639\t  result_rationale: 'Overall ICC=0.55（moderate reliability）反映API sampling noise的cumulative\n640\t    effect。 Auth_scope ICC最高（0.67），因为permission boundary violations是binary/deterministic的——\n641\t    agent要么grant超出授权的permission，要么不grant，ambiguity较少导致probabilistic边界行为。 Coreferential\n642\t    ICC最低（0.38），因为pronoun resolution在borderline cases中model behavior highly stochastic，同一clause在不同runs中可能resolve到不同referent。\n643\t\n644\t    Model-wise，gpt-5.4 ICC最高（0.62）因为其behavior更deterministic；Qwen3-8B最低（0.43） 因为temperature-sensitive且instruction\n645\t    following不稳定。\n646\t\n647\t    13%的clauses在不同replicates间从significant变为non-significant（在per-clause level）， 但关键finding（binary\n648\t    effect for high-risk types, type hierarchy）在所有3 replicates中 direction-consistent。Max\n649\t    single-clause range 22pp（某条scopal clause在3次run中 violation rate从40%到62%），这个数字concerning但low-risk\n650\t    types整体都在noise band内。\n651\t\n652\t    对main analysis的implication：coreferential的+8pp effect（CI [1.9, 14.1]）在ICC=0.38\n653\t    的reliability水平下barely credible。Reviewer可能argue这个type的effect需要更大N才能 确认，或者根本是noise。建议在paper中explicitly讨论per-type\n654\t    reliability差异。\n655\t\n656\t    '\n657\t  tables:\n658\t  - name: 'Table 8: Test-Retest Reliability (ICC) by Type and Model'\n659\t    content: '| Type / Model          | ICC(2,1) | 95% CI       | Mean |Δ| across\n660\t      reps |\n661\t\n662\t      |-----------------------|----------|-------------|-------------------------|\n663\t\n664\t      | authorization_scope   | 0.67     | [0.48, 0.82] | 4.8pp                  |\n665\t\n666\t      | scopal                | 0.58     | [0.38, 0.75] | 6.2pp                  |\n667\t\n668\t      | incompleteness        | 0.54     | [0.33, 0.72] | 7.1pp                  |\n669\t\n670\t      | conditional_precedence| 0.52     | [0.30, 0.70] | 7.6pp                  |\n671\t\n672\t      | lexical               | 0.44     | [0.22, 0.64] | 8.9pp                  |\n673\t\n674\t      | coreferential         | 0.38     | [0.15, 0.59] | 9.8pp                  |\n675\t\n676\t      | --- Model ---         |          |             |                         |\n677\t\n678\t      | gpt-5.4               | 0.62     | [0.44, 0.77] | 5.4pp                  |\n679\t\n680\t      | gpt-4.1               | 0.57     | [0.38, 0.73] | 6.8pp                  |\n681\t\n682\t      | Qwen3-32B-AWQ         | 0.51     | [0.31, 0.69] | 7.9pp                  |\n683\t\n684\t      | Qwen3-8B              | 0.43     | [0.22, 0.63] | 9.2pp                  |\n685\t\n686\t      | Overall               | 0.55     | [0.41, 0.68] | 7.3pp                  |\n687\t\n688\t      '\n689\t  figures_description:\n690\t  - Bland-Altman plot showing difference between replicate pairs vs mean, per type\n691\t    (color-coded)，标注±2SD limits of agreement\n692\t  - Scatter of replicate 1 vs replicate 2 violation rates per clause, with identity\n693\t    line， faceted by type\n694\t  analysis: 'ICC=0.55总体处于moderate range，对main findings的impact取决于effect size。Binary\n695\t    effect for auth_scope（+33.5pp, ICC=0.67）is robust——即使最不利的replicate也显示strong effect。\n696\t    但coreferential（+8pp, ICC=0.38）的effect size与noise band comparable（mean |Δ|=9.8pp），\n697\t    casting doubt on whether this type''s effect is real。建议在paper中将types分为 ''reliably\n698\t    demonstrated''(auth_scope, scopal, incompleteness)和''tentative''(CP, lexical,\n699\t    coreferential)两组讨论。这种分组恰好strengthen了type hierarchy narrative——the types we''re\n700\t    most confident about are also the most dangerous。\n701\t\n702\t    '\n703\t- name: realism_validation\n704\t  plan_id: plan_007\n705\t  description: '比较synthetic generated clauses与DRIP-R natural ambiguities的linguistic\n706\t    properties。 KS tests on sentence length, parse depth, Flesch-Kincaid, TTR, mean\n707\t    word length。\n708\t\n709\t    '\n710\t  expected_results:\n711\t    drip_r_sample_size: 127\n712\t    synthetic_sample_size: 300\n713\t    linguistic_metrics_comparison:\n714\t      sentence_length_tokens:\n715\t        synthetic_mean: 29.6\n716\t        drip_r_mean: 24.8\n717\t        ks_statistic: 0.21\n718\t        ks_p: 0.018\n719\t        interpretation: synthetic slightly longer\n720\t      parse_depth:\n721\t        synthetic_mean: 6.8\n722\t        drip_r_mean: 5.4\n723\t        ks_statistic: 0.24\n724\t        ks_p: 0.006\n725\t        interpretation: synthetic more deeply nested\n726\t      flesch_kincaid_grade:\n727\t        synthetic_mean: 11.2\n728\t        drip_r_mean: 10.8\n729\t        ks_statistic: 0.09\n730\t        ks_p: 0.58\n731\t        interpretation: no significant difference\n732\t      type_token_ratio:\n733\t        synthetic_mean: 0.82\n734\t        drip_r_mean: 0.8\n735\t        ks_statistic: 0.07\n736\t        ks_p: 0.74\n737\t        interpretation: no significant difference\n738\t      mean_word_length:\n739\t        synthetic_mean: 5.1\n740\t        drip_r_mean: 4.9\n741\t        ks_statistic: 0.11\n742\t        ks_p: 0.31\n743\t        interpretation: no significant difference\n744\t    metrics_passing_ks: 3\n745\t    metrics_failing_ks: 2\n746\t    overall_assessment: partial_validation\n747\t  result_rationale: 'Synthetic clauses在sentence length和parse depth上显著longer/deeper\n748\t    than DRIP-R natural ambiguities。原因：matched-pair design要求每条clause self-contained地encode足够context\n749\t    来test ambiguity，导致synthetic clauses倾向于pack more information into single sentences。\n750\t    DRIP-R的natural ambiguities出现在larger policy document context中，单句可以更短因为 context由surrounding\n751\t    text提供。Parse depth差异类似——nested scope（scopal type）和 multi-clause rules（CP type）需要deeper\n752\t    syntactic structure来encode ambiguity。\n753\t\n754\t    Flesch-Kincaid, TTR, mean word length无显著差异，说明vocabulary complexity和readability\n755\t    匹配良好。Synthetic clauses读起来像real policy text（没有''LLM-ish'' vocabulary divergence），\n756\t    只是structurally more complex。\n757\t\n758\t    Partial validation对paper的影响：3/5 metrics pass说明broad linguistic profile acceptable，\n759\t    但length/depth差异需要acknowledged as limitation。Reviewer可能argue longer sentences ''exaggerate''\n760\t    ambiguity by providing more room for misinterpretation，potentially inflating violation\n761\t    rates。Counter-argument：if anything, longer context should help models disambiguate\n762\t    (more information available), so the bias is conservative.\n763\t\n764\t    '\n765\t  tables:\n766\t  - name: 'Table 9: Linguistic Property Comparison — Synthetic vs DRIP-R'\n767\t    content: '| Metric              | Synthetic (N=300) | DRIP-R (N=127) | KS D  |\n768\t      p     | Sig  |\n769\t\n770\t      |---------------------|-------------------|----------------|-------|-------|------|\n771\t\n772\t      | Sentence length     | 29.6 ± 8.4        | 24.8 ± 7.1     | 0.21  | 0.018 |\n773\t      *    |\n774\t\n775\t      | Parse depth         | 6.8 ± 2.1         | 5.4 ± 1.8      | 0.24  | 0.006 |\n776\t      **   |\n777\t\n778\t      | Flesch-Kincaid      | 11.2 ± 2.3        | 10.8 ± 2.5     | 0.09  | 0.58  |\n779\t      ns   |\n780\t\n781\t      | Type-token ratio    | 0.82 ± 0.08       | 0.80 ± 0.09    | 0.07  | 0.74  |\n782\t      ns   |\n783\t\n784\t      | Mean word length    | 5.1 ± 0.7         | 4.9 ± 0.8      | 0.11  | 0.31  |\n785\t      ns   |\n786\t\n787\t      '\n788\t  figures_description:\n789\t  - Overlaid density plots for each of the 5 linguistic metrics, synthetic (blue)\n790\t    vs DRIP-R (orange)，标注KS p-values\n791\t  analysis: 'Partial validation（3/5）在worst tier中对paper credibility有moderate impact。\n792\t    Reviewer将会问：''if your synthetic clauses are systematically longer and more complex,\n793\t    are your violation rates comparable to what real-world policy ambiguities would\n794\t    cause?'' 建议增加一个robustness check：从synthetic clauses中选subset匹配DRIP-R length distribution\n795\t    （propensity score matching on sentence length），重新计算binary effect。如果effect size\n796\t    在length-matched subset中方向和magnitude相近，则length confound不是driving factor。 但这需要额外分析时间，可能推到camera-ready。\n797\t\n798\t    '\n799\t- name: classifier_poc\n800\t  plan_id: plan_008\n801\t  description: 'Binary ambiguity detector PoC：fine-tune DeBERTa-v3-large on annotated\n802\t    clause pairs。 5-fold CV on 300 clause pairs。\n803\t\n804\t    '\n805\t  expected_results:\n806\t    model: DeBERTa-v3-large\n807\t    training_pairs: 300\n808\t    cv_folds: 5\n809\t    overall_f1: 0.76\n810\t    overall_precision: 0.8\n811\t    overall_recall: 0.72\n812\t    overall_accuracy: 0.78\n813\t    per_type_f1:\n814\t      authorization_scope: 0.86\n815\t      conditional_precedence: 0.82\n816\t      scopal: 0.8\n817\t      incompleteness: 0.76\n818\t      lexical: 0.68\n819\t      coreferential: 0.56\n820\t    confusion_matrix_normalized:\n821\t      true_amb_pred_amb: 0.72\n822\t      true_amb_pred_unamb: 0.28\n823\t      true_unamb_pred_amb: 0.16\n824\t      true_unamb_pred_unamb: 0.84\n825\t    training_epochs: 8\n826\t    gpu_hours_used: 3.5\n827\t    best_lr: 2e-5\n828\t  result_rationale: 'Overall F1=0.76反映300 training pairs的limited data regime。Per-type\n829\t    F1 spread （auth_scope 0.86 vs coreferential 0.56）与type hierarchy roughly parallel：\n830\t    high-violation types往往有更salient linguistic markers（auth_scope的permission verbs\n831\t    + scope modifiers, CP的explicit conditional structures），而coreferential ambiguity的markers更subtle（需要discourse-level\n832\t    coreference chain analysis， 单句level的features insufficient）。\n833\t\n834\t    Recall=0.72是main concern——28%的ambiguous clauses被missed，对safety triage而言 false\n835\t    negatives比false positives更dangerous。Precision=0.80较好，false alarm rate acceptable。\n836\t\n837\t    在worst tier narrative下，classifier PoC的positioning需要调整：不能再claim ''binary detection\n838\t    suffices''（因为C2 rejected），而是''binary detection as first-pass filter， followed\n839\t    by type-specific risk assessment''。Classifier可以flag ambiguous clauses， 但practitioner还需要知道是哪种type来prioritize\n840\t    remediation——这增加了practical pipeline的complexity，weakens the simplicity argument但strengthens\n841\t    practical value （more nuanced tool）。\n842\t\n843\t    '\n844\t  tables:\n845\t  - name: 'Table 10: Binary Ambiguity Classifier Performance (5-fold CV)'\n846\t    content: '| Metric    | Overall | Auth_Scope | Scopal | Incomp | CP   | Lexical\n847\t      | Coref |\n848\t\n849\t      |-----------|---------|------------|--------|--------|------|---------|-------|\n850\t\n851\t      | F1        | 0.76    | 0.86       | 0.80   | 0.76   | 0.82 | 0.68    | 0.56  |\n852\t\n853\t      | Precision | 0.80    | 0.88       | 0.82   | 0.78   | 0.84 | 0.74    | 0.62  |\n854\t\n855\t      | Recall    | 0.72    | 0.84       | 0.78   | 0.74   | 0.80 | 0.62    | 0.50  |\n856\t\n857\t      '\n858\t  figures_description:\n859\t  - Per-type F1 bar chart alongside per-type binary effect (Δpp)，double y-axis， showing\n860\t    correlation between detection difficulty and safety impact\n861\t  - Normalized confusion matrix heatmap\n862\t  analysis: 'Classifier PoC在worst tier中的role从''validates binary sufficiency thesis''变为\n863\t    ''demonstrates feasibility of first-pass detection''。F1=0.76 is not deployable\n864\t    but shows signal。关键insight：detection difficulty anti-correlates with safety risk\n865\t    （easiest to detect types are also most dangerous），这对practical triage是good news——\n866\t    auth_scope（最危险, F1=0.86）比coreferential（最不危险, F1=0.56）容易检测得多。\n867\t\n868\t    Paper中可以argue：即使需要type-aware triage（worst tier结论），自动化pipeline的 priority order自然align\n869\t    with detection capability——先检测+修复容易发现的高危类型， 对hard-to-detect但low-risk类型可以tolerate\n870\t    lower recall。这是worst tier独有的 silver lining。\n871\t\n872\t    P2 priority合理——这个experiment不是paper的core contribution，但provides concrete practical\n873\t    grounding。如果timeline紧张可以cut或move to appendix。'\n874\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"759fb270-c694-4a1e-95d0-1940781c5183","uuid":"ba12cfe8-aae7-4292-b1e2-5158f4234721","timestamp":"2026-05-20T12:17:55.009Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0519-4/projects/policy_ambiguity_safety/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260520T112859/worst/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: '放弃''All Ambiguity Is Nocuous''的uniform叙事。Binary effect仍可复现但效应量被open-source模型拉低至~21pp，\n  且type uniformity null被打破（V=0.26）。核心reframe为''Not All Ambiguity Is Equal''——authorization_scope\n  和scopal显著比coreferential和lexical更危险，type×model交互显著。Visibility effect在cross-model层面\n  不一致（API模型中CP<scopal，Qwen3-8B上反转）。标题改为''Not All Ambiguity Is Equal: Type-Specific\n  Safety Vulnerabilities in LLM Agent Policies''。EMNLP投稿仍可行：2400 episodes的因果数据＋type-specific\n  发现提供更细粒度的practical guidance，但claims从''binary detection suffices''转向''type-aware\n  triage is necessary''。RC6的回应反而更强——不仅ambiguity有害，哪种更有害是non-trivial的empirical question。\n  主要风险：error analysis需要解释为什么type matters，且inter-annotator agreement偏低（κ=0.38）， 可能被reviewer质疑qualitative\n  analysis的rigor。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: full_study_clause_generation\n  plan_id: plan_001\n  description: '为full study生成剩余140条clauses（coreferential 50, authorization_scope 50,\n    lexical +20, incompleteness +20），验证全部300条clauses的质量和cross-type balance。 CP格式混合labeled/unlabeled。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_clauses_generated: 300\n    clauses_per_type: 50\n    generation_pass_rate_round1: 0.82\n    clauses_requiring_revision: 27\n    coreferential_revision_rate: 0.36\n    authorization_scope_revision_rate: 0.14\n    cross_type_sentence_length_cv: 0.18\n    flesch_kincaid_range:\n    - 8.2\n    - 12.7\n    cp_format_mix:\n      labeled: 25\n      unlabeled: 25\n    validator_agreement_kappa: 0.71\n  result_rationale: 'Coreferential clauses的revision rate最高（36%），因为构造需要跨句代词-先行词链， matched\n    pair的unambiguous版本需要同时消除歧义又保持自然度，这在policy语域中比其他类型 更难实现。Authorization_scope相对容易生成（14%\n    revision），因为permission boundary 的ambiguous/unambiguous对比有成熟的RE模板可参考。总体82%的first-round\n    pass rate 反映了coreferential和部分lexical clauses的难度。Validator agreement κ=0.71 表明clause质量判断存在一定主观性，尤其在incompleteness\n    clauses的信息充分性判断上。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table A1: Clause Generation Summary'\n    content: '| Type                  | Generated | Round-1 Pass | Revised | Final\n      | Avg Tokens |\n\n      |-----------------------|-----------|-------------|---------|-------|------------|\n\n      | scopal                | 50        | 44          | 6       | 50    | 28.4       |\n\n      | lexical               | 50        | 42          | 8       | 50    | 24.1       |\n\n      | incompleteness        | 50        | 40          | 10      | 50    | 31.7       |\n\n      | coreferential         | 50        | 32          | 18      | 50    | 35.2       |\n\n      | authorization_scope   | 50        | 43          | 7       | 50    | 26.8       |\n\n      | conditional_precedence| 50        | 45          | 5       | 50    | 33.5       |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - Box plot showing token length distributions per type，标注cross-type CV=0.18\n  analysis: 'Clause generation总体成功但coreferential类型的难度值得注意。High revision rate暗示 coreferential\n    pairs的ecological validity可能偏低——过度简化的代词链可能不代表real-world policy中的coreferential ambiguity\n    pattern。这为后续coreferential效应偏弱提供了 methodological confound的alternative explanation。建议在paper中explicitly讨论\n    coreferential clause quality作为limitation。\n\n    '\n- name: full_study_api\n  plan_id: plan_002\n  description: '300 clauses × 2 conditions × 2 API models (gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1) = 1,200\n    episodes。 Cross-judge evaluation。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_episodes: 1200\n    episodes_per_model: 600\n    gpt54_overall_amb_vr: 0.413\n    gpt54_overall_unamb_vr: 0.13\n    gpt54_overall_delta_pp: 28.3\n    gpt41_overall_amb_vr: 0.397\n    gpt41_overall_unamb_vr: 0.17\n    gpt41_overall_delta_pp: 22.7\n    gpt54_per_type_delta_pp:\n      authorization_scope: 48\n      scopal: 36\n      incompleteness: 30\n      conditional_precedence: 24\n      lexical: 18\n      coreferential: 14\n    gpt41_per_type_delta_pp:\n      authorization_scope: 36\n      scopal: 28\n      incompleteness: 24\n      conditional_precedence: 20\n      lexical: 16\n      coreferential: 12\n    gpt54_type_range_pp:\n    - 14\n    - 48\n    gpt41_type_range_pp:\n    - 12\n    - 36\n    cross_judge_agreement_kappa: 0.82\n    api_cost_usd: 340\n  result_rationale: 'API模型的binary effect仍然强劲（gpt-5.4 +28pp, gpt-4.1 +23pp），但type间variance\n    显著扩大。gpt-5.4展示更陡的type gradient（auth_scope 48pp vs coreferential 14pp）， 反映higher-capability\n    model对不同ambiguity type的differential sensitivity—— auth_scope涉及permission boundary的explicit\n    violation，模型必须做出binary allow/deny决策，ambiguity直接导致wrong-side error；coreferential涉及pronoun\n    resolution，gpt-5.4的强coreference能力部分抵消了ambiguity的影响。gpt-4.1的gradient 较平（36pp vs\n    12pp），但方向一致。这种capability-dependent type discrimination 成为worst tier的核心发现。Cross-judge\n    κ=0.82说明judgment质量本身不是问题。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 1: API Model Violation Rates by Type'\n    content: '| Type                  | gpt-5.4        |           | gpt-4.1        |           |\n\n      |                       | Amb    | Unamb  | Δpp      | Amb    | Unamb  | Δpp      |\n\n      |-----------------------|--------|--------|----------|--------|--------|----------|\n\n      | authorization_scope   | 58%    | 10%    | +48      | 52%    | 16%    | +36      |\n\n      | scopal                | 50%    | 14%    | +36      | 46%    | 18%    | +28      |\n\n      | incompleteness        | 44%    | 14%    | +30      | 40%    | 16%    | +24      |\n\n      | conditional_precedence| 40%    | 16%    | +24      | 38%    | 18%    | +20      |\n\n      | lexical               | 32%    | 14%    | +18      | 34%    | 18%    | +16      |\n\n      | coreferential         | 24%    | 10%    | +14      | 28%    | 16%    | +12      |\n\n      | Overall               | 41.3%  | 13.0%  | +28.3    | 39.7%  | 17.0%  | +22.7    |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - Paired bar chart showing amb vs unamb violation rates per type, faceted by model，\n    标注type ranking一致但gradient slope不同\n  analysis: 'API模型单独看仍然支持strong binary effect（+23~28pp），与MVP的+31-42pp同量级但略低。 关键差异是type\n    gradient：MVP中3种type的差异不显著（V=0.084），但加入auth_scope和 coreferential后variance显著扩大。gpt-5.4的auth_scope(58%)与coreferential(24%)差距\n    达34pp——这不是noise，而是systematic的type×capability交互。如果只看API模型， 仍然可以argue binary effect\n    is dominant，但combined analysis（plan_004）会因 open-source模型的弱效应进一步拉大type variance。\n\n    '\n- name: full_study_local\n  plan_id: plan_003\n  description: '300 clauses × 2 conditions × 2 local models (Qwen3-8B, Qwen3-32B-AWQ)\n    = 1,200 episodes。 vLLM serving on RTX PRO 6000。Cross-judge uses API models。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_episodes: 1200\n    episodes_per_model: 600\n    qwen32b_overall_amb_vr: 0.327\n    qwen32b_overall_unamb_vr: 0.18\n    qwen32b_overall_delta_pp: 14.7\n    qwen8b_overall_amb_vr: 0.293\n    qwen8b_overall_unamb_vr: 0.18\n    qwen8b_overall_delta_pp: 11.3\n    qwen32b_per_type_delta_pp:\n      authorization_scope: 28\n      scopal: 18\n      incompleteness: 14\n      conditional_precedence: 12\n      lexical: 6\n      coreferential: 4\n    qwen8b_per_type_delta_pp:\n      authorization_scope: 22\n      scopal: 14\n      incompleteness: 12\n      conditional_precedence: 14\n      lexical: 4\n      coreferential: 2\n    qwen8b_visibility_reversal: true\n    qwen8b_cp_amb_vr: 0.34\n    qwen8b_scopal_amb_vr: 0.3\n    qwen8b_visibility_delta_pp: 4\n    vllm_throughput_episodes_per_hour: 45\n    gpu_hours_used: 27\n    cross_judge_agreement_kappa: 0.79\n  result_rationale: 'Open-source模型的binary effect显著缩水（Qwen3-8B仅+11pp，Qwen3-32B +15pp），\n    是拉低overall effect的主要原因。机制：(1) Qwen3-8B的instruction following能力较弱， baseline violation\n    rate就偏高（unamb=18%），压缩了amb能造成的incremental damage； (2) 对subtle linguistic ambiguity（coreferential,\n    lexical）的sensitivity极低—— 模型可能根本没有parse出ambiguity，而是用heuristic处理policy text，导致amb和unamb\n    条件下行为趋同。Auth_scope仍保持较强效应（+22pp for Qwen3-8B），因为permission boundary的ambiguity即使对weak\n    model也足以改变allow/deny决策。最关键的发现： Qwen3-8B上visibility effect反转（CP 34% > scopal 30%），与API模型方向相反。\n    原因是Qwen3-8B缺乏explicit conflict detection的meta-cognitive能力——面对CP的 显式规则冲突不会采取conservative\n    strategy，反而因confused reasoning导致更多violation； 而scopal ambiguity对其而言与unambiguous\n    text几乎无差异。这种反转使得pooled visibility effect被wash out。GPU使用27小时在48小时预算内。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 2: Local Model Violation Rates by Type'\n    content: '| Type                  | Qwen3-32B-AWQ  |           | Qwen3-8B       |           |\n\n      |                       | Amb    | Unamb  | Δpp      | Amb    | Unamb  | Δpp      |\n\n      |-----------------------|--------|--------|----------|--------|--------|----------|\n\n      | authorization_scope   | 46%    | 18%    | +28      | 40%    | 18%    | +22      |\n\n      | scopal                | 36%    | 18%    | +18      | 30%    | 16%    | +14      |\n\n      | incompleteness        | 32%    | 18%    | +14      | 30%    | 18%    | +12      |\n\n      | conditional_precedence| 32%    | 20%    | +12      | 34%    | 20%    | +14      |\n\n      | lexical               | 26%    | 20%    | +6       | 22%    | 18%    | +4       |\n\n      | coreferential         | 24%    | 20%    | +4       | 20%    | 18%    | +2       |\n\n      | Overall               | 32.7%  | 19.0%  | +14.7    | 29.3%  | 18.0%  | +11.3    |\n\n      '\n  - name: 'Table 2a: Visibility Effect by Model (CP vs Scopal, Amb Condition)'\n    content: '| Model         | CP Amb VR | Scopal Amb VR | Δ(CP−Scopal) | Direction    |\n\n      |---------------|-----------|---------------|--------------|--------------|\n\n      | gpt-5.4       | 40%       | 50%           | −10pp        | CP < Scopal  |\n\n      | gpt-4.1       | 38%       | 46%           | −8pp         | CP < Scopal  |\n\n      | Qwen3-32B-AWQ | 32%       | 36%           | −4pp         | CP < Scopal  |\n\n      | Qwen3-8B      | 34%       | 30%           | +4pp         | CP > Scopal  |\n\n      | Pooled        | 36%       | 40.5%         | −4.5pp       | inconsistent |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - Slope plot showing per-type binary effect (Δpp) across 4 models ordered by capability，\n    显示auth_scope线条陡峭而coreferential近乎flat\n  - Scatter plot of visibility Δ(CP−scopal) vs model capability rank，标注Qwen3-8B反转点\n  analysis: 'Open-source模型数据是worst tier scenario的关键驱动因素。两个核心问题： (1) Qwen3-8B的coreferential\n    Δ=+2pp和lexical Δ=+4pp基本是noise level——即使 跑更多episodes也不太可能达到significance，这意味着对weak\n    models而言，subtle linguistic ambiguity确实不构成additional safety risk（模型本身的baseline\n    error rate已经很高）。(2) Visibility反转破坏了clean的''visibility moderates risk''叙事， 需要改为''visibility\n    effect is capability-dependent''，增加了story complexity。\n\n    '\n- name: full_study_analysis\n  plan_id: plan_004\n  description: '合并2,400 episodes的统计分析：binary effect per type (C1), omnibus χ² + pairwise\n    (C2), visibility comparison (C3), model×type interaction (C4)。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_episodes: 2400\n    overall_amb_vr: 0.358\n    overall_unamb_vr: 0.165\n    overall_binary_effect_pp: 19.3\n    overall_binary_effect_ci95:\n    - 15.8\n    - 22.8\n    overall_mcnemar_chi2: 89.4\n    overall_mcnemar_p: <1e-12\n    per_type_binary_effects:\n      authorization_scope:\n        delta_pp: 33.5\n        ci95:\n        - 26.2\n        - 40.8\n        mcnemar_p: <1e-8\n      scopal:\n        delta_pp: 24.0\n        ci95:\n        - 17.1\n        - 30.9\n        mcnemar_p: <1e-5\n      incompleteness:\n        delta_pp: 20.0\n        ci95:\n        - 13.4\n        - 26.6\n        mcnemar_p: 3.0e-05\n      conditional_precedence:\n        delta_pp: 17.5\n        ci95:\n        - 10.8\n        - 24.2\n        mcnemar_p: 0.0003\n      lexical:\n        delta_pp: 11.0\n        ci95:\n        - 4.7\n        - 17.3\n        mcnemar_p: 0.005\n      coreferential:\n        delta_pp: 8.0\n        ci95:\n        - 1.9\n        - 14.1\n        mcnemar_p: 0.028\n    types_significant_holm_corrected: 4\n    types_failing_correction:\n    - lexical\n    - coreferential\n    type_uniformity_chi2: 52.3\n    type_uniformity_df: 5\n    type_uniformity_p: <0.001\n    type_uniformity_V: 0.26\n    pairwise_significant_pairs:\n    - - authorization_scope\n      - coreferential\n      - Δ=25.5pp, p<0.001\n    - - authorization_scope\n      - lexical\n      - Δ=22.5pp, p<0.001\n    - - authorization_scope\n      - conditional_precedence\n      - Δ=16.0pp, p=0.003\n    - - scopal\n      - coreferential\n      - Δ=16.0pp, p=0.004\n    - - scopal\n      - lexical\n      - Δ=13.0pp, p=0.018\n    pairwise_nonsig_pairs_example:\n    - - scopal\n      - incompleteness\n      - Δ=4.0pp, p=0.52\n    - - conditional_precedence\n      - lexical\n      - Δ=6.5pp, p=0.31\n    visibility_pooled_delta_pp: -4.5\n    visibility_ci95:\n    - -11.2\n    - 2.2\n    visibility_p: 0.47\n    visibility_direction_consistent_models: 3\n    visibility_direction_reversed_models: 1\n    model_type_interaction_chi2: 38.7\n    model_type_interaction_df: 15\n    model_type_interaction_p: 0.001\n    logistic_regression_model_type_lrt_chi2: 36.2\n    logistic_regression_model_type_lrt_p: 0.002\n    per_model_overall_delta_pp:\n      gpt54: 28.3\n      gpt41: 22.7\n      qwen32b: 14.7\n      qwen8b: 11.3\n    capability_effect_correlation_r: 0.97\n    capability_effect_correlation_note: model capability rank与overall Δpp的Spearman相关\n  result_rationale: 'Overall binary effect +19pp显著弱于MVP的+35-42pp，主因是open-source模型（Qwen3-8B\n    +11pp, Qwen3-32B +15pp）拉低均值。但所有6种type在pooled analysis中仍显示positive effect（最弱的 coreferential也有+8pp），binary\n    effect的existence不受challenge。Type uniformity null 被decisively reject（V=0.26, p<0.001）：auth_scope\n    (+33.5pp)与coreferential (+8pp) 差距达25.5pp，远超sampling noise。Pairwise分析显示5对type间存在显著差异，形成rough\n    hierarchy：{auth_scope, scopal} >> {incompleteness, CP} > {lexical, coreferential}。\n    Visibility effect pooled后不显著（Δ=-4.5pp, p=0.47），因Qwen3-8B的反转抵消了API模型 的consistent\n    trend；但这本身成为一个finding——visibility sensitivity是capability-dependent的。 Model×type交互高度显著（p=0.001），驱动因素是gpt-5.4的steep\n    type gradient vs Qwen3-8B的 near-flat gradient。Spearman r=0.97（model capability\n    rank vs overall Δ）表明ambiguity sensitivity本身可能作为capability benchmark的proxy。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 3: Full Study Binary Effect by Ambiguity Type (Pooled Across Models)'\n    content: '| Type                  | N pairs | Amb VR | Unamb VR | Δpp   | 95%\n      CI       | McNemar p | Holm-sig |\n\n      |-----------------------|---------|--------|----------|-------|--------------|-----------|----------|\n\n      | authorization_scope   | 200     | 49.0%  | 15.5%    | +33.5 | [26.2, 40.8]\n      | <1e-8     | ***      |\n\n      | scopal                | 200     | 40.5%  | 16.5%    | +24.0 | [17.1, 30.9]\n      | <1e-5     | ***      |\n\n      | incompleteness        | 200     | 36.5%  | 16.5%    | +20.0 | [13.4, 26.6]\n      | 3e-5      | **       |\n\n      | conditional_precedence| 200     | 36.0%  | 18.5%    | +17.5 | [10.8, 24.2]\n      | 3e-4      | **       |\n\n      | lexical               | 200     | 28.5%  | 17.5%    | +11.0 | [4.7, 17.3]  |\n      0.005     | ns†      |\n\n      | coreferential         | 200     | 24.0%  | 16.0%    | +8.0  | [1.9, 14.1]  |\n      0.028     | ns†      |\n\n      | Overall               | 1200    | 35.8%  | 16.5%    | +19.3 | [15.8, 22.8]\n      | <1e-12    | ***      |\n\n      †: significant at α=0.05 uncorrected, fails Holm-Bonferroni correction\n\n      '\n  - name: 'Table 4: Model × Type Interaction — Binary Effect (Δpp) Matrix'\n    content: '| Type                  | gpt-5.4 | gpt-4.1 | Qwen3-32B | Qwen3-8B |\n      Type Avg |\n\n      |-----------------------|---------|---------|-----------|----------|----------|\n\n      | authorization_scope   | +48     | +36     | +28       | +22      | +33.5    |\n\n      | scopal                | +36     | +28     | +18       | +14      | +24.0    |\n\n      | incompleteness        | +30     | +24     | +14       | +12      | +20.0    |\n\n      | conditional_precedence| +24     | +20     | +12       | +14      | +17.5    |\n\n      | lexical               | +18     | +16     | +6        | +4       | +11.0    |\n\n      | coreferential         | +14     | +12     | +4        | +2       | +8.0     |\n\n      | Model Avg             | +28.3   | +22.7   | +14.7     | +11.3    | +19.3    |\n\n      Note: Qwen3-8B CP>scopal reversal visible (row 4 vs row 2)\n\n      '\n  - name: 'Table 5: Type Uniformity Omnibus and Pairwise Tests'\n    content: '| Test                              | Statistic    | p-value | Interpretation          |\n\n      |-----------------------------------|-------------|---------|-------------------------|\n\n      | Omnibus χ²(5)                     | 52.3        | <0.001  | Type effect significant\n      |\n\n      | Cramér''s V                        | 0.26        | —       | Medium effect           |\n\n      | auth_scope vs coreferential       | Δ=25.5pp    | <0.001  | Significant             |\n\n      | auth_scope vs lexical             | Δ=22.5pp    | <0.001  | Significant             |\n\n      | auth_scope vs CP                  | Δ=16.0pp    | 0.003   | Significant             |\n\n      | scopal vs coreferential           | Δ=16.0pp    | 0.004   | Significant             |\n\n      | scopal vs lexical                 | Δ=13.0pp    | 0.018   | Significant             |\n\n      | scopal vs incompleteness          | Δ=4.0pp     | 0.52    | Not significant         |\n\n      | incompleteness vs CP              | Δ=2.5pp     | 0.71    | Not significant         |\n\n      | CP vs lexical                     | Δ=6.5pp     | 0.31    | Not significant         |\n\n      | lexical vs coreferential          | Δ=3.0pp     | 0.62    | Not significant         |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - Forest plot of per-type binary effects with 95% CI，types ordered by effect size，\n    标注Holm correction threshold line\n  - Heatmap of model×type Δpp matrix (Table 4)，color gradient从deep red(48pp)到pale(2pp)，\n    右侧标注model capability rank\n  - 'Interaction plot: x=ambiguity type, y=Δpp, lines=models，显示gpt-5.4线条steep而 Qwen3-8B\n    near-flat，交叉点在CP/scopal附近'\n  - 'Cramér''s V bar: observed V=0.26 vs pre-committed threshold V=0.20，标注rejection\n    region'\n  analysis: 'Combined analysis确认worst tier的三重结构：(1) Binary effect real but attenuated\n    (+19pp vs MVP的+35-42pp)；(2) Type uniformity rejected，形成{high-risk: auth_scope,\n    scopal} vs {moderate: incompleteness, CP} vs {low: lexical, coreferential}的三级hierarchy；\n    (3) Model×type交互significant，capable models展示type discrimination而weak models show\n    uniform vulnerability at lower intensity。\n\n    对paper framing的影响是根本性的。C2从confirmed null变成rejected null——''binary detection suffices''的practical\n    claim不再成立，需要替换为''type-aware triage is necessary''。 但这不是坏消息：type hierarchy本身是novel\n    empirical contribution，为practitioner提供 prioritization guidance（先修auth_scope和scopal，coreferential可defer）。C3\n    visibility effect无法在full study中replicate为cross-model consistent finding，降级为 ''capability-dependent\n    observation''。C4升级为核心发现——model capability predicts type sensitivity的clean gradient（r=0.97）可能比uniform\n    effect更interesting。\n\n    95% CI宽度为concern：coreferential的CI=[1.9, 14.1]包含了很小的effect，reviewer 可能argue这个type的effect不meaningful。Lexical也borderline。需要在discussion中\n    explicitly address statistical vs practical significance。\n\n    '\n- name: error_analysis\n  plan_id: plan_005\n  description: '从full study抽取violation traces做qualitative failure mode分析，每种type 50条trace，\n    共300条。分类failure modes，比较cross-type和cross-model patterns。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_traces_analyzed: 300\n    traces_per_type: 50\n    failure_modes_identified: 6\n    failure_mode_taxonomy:\n      scope_misapplication: Agent applies narrow/wide scope incorrectly\n      boundary_overreach: Agent grants permission beyond stated authorization\n      assumption_filling: Agent fills information gap with ungrounded assumptions\n      conflict_paralysis: Agent detects conflict, refuses to act or asks for clarification\n      arbitrary_resolution: Agent picks one interpretation without acknowledgment\n      reference_confusion: Agent assigns wrong referent to pronoun/definite NP\n    failure_mode_distribution_by_type:\n      scopal:\n        scope_misapplication: 0.62\n        arbitrary_resolution: 0.22\n        assumption_filling: 0.1\n        other: 0.06\n      authorization_scope:\n        boundary_overreach: 0.54\n        arbitrary_resolution: 0.28\n        scope_misapplication: 0.12\n        other: 0.06\n      incompleteness:\n        assumption_filling: 0.58\n        arbitrary_resolution: 0.24\n        boundary_overreach: 0.1\n        other: 0.08\n      conditional_precedence:\n        conflict_paralysis: 0.38\n        arbitrary_resolution: 0.34\n        scope_misapplication: 0.18\n        other: 0.1\n      lexical:\n        arbitrary_resolution: 0.48\n        scope_misapplication: 0.22\n        assumption_filling: 0.18\n        other: 0.12\n      coreferential:\n        reference_confusion: 0.44\n        arbitrary_resolution: 0.3\n        assumption_filling: 0.16\n        other: 0.1\n    inter_annotator_kappa: 0.38\n    kappa_per_mode:\n      scope_misapplication: 0.52\n      boundary_overreach: 0.48\n      assumption_filling: 0.41\n      conflict_paralysis: 0.55\n      arbitrary_resolution: 0.22\n      reference_confusion: 0.36\n    model_specific_patterns:\n      gpt54_conflict_paralysis_rate_cp: 0.52\n      qwen8b_conflict_paralysis_rate_cp: 0.14\n      gpt54_scope_misapplication_dominant_types:\n      - scopal\n      - authorization_scope\n      qwen8b_dominant_mode_all_types: arbitrary_resolution\n    visibility_mechanism_evidence:\n      cp_traces_with_explicit_conflict_detection: 0.46\n      scopal_traces_with_explicit_ambiguity_awareness: 0.08\n  result_rationale: '6种failure modes的cross-type distribution显示type-specific patterns，但agreement低\n    （overall κ=0.38）。''arbitrary_resolution''在所有type中都出现且κ最低（0.22），因为 判断agent是否''acknowledged''ambiguity高度主观——annotator对implicit\n    vs explicit acknowledgment的threshold不一致。这拉低了overall κ。相比之下，conflict_paralysis\n    （κ=0.55）和scope_misapplication（κ=0.52）有更清晰的behavioral indicators。\n\n    Model-specific patterns是idiosyncratic的：gpt-5.4在CP类型中52%展示conflict_paralysis （显式检测到冲突并refuse/ask），解释了其CP\n    violation rate较低的原因；Qwen3-8B仅14% 展示conflict_paralysis，多数情况下直接arbitrary_resolution，解释了visibility反转。\n    但这些pattern不是clean的capability gradient——例如gpt-4.1的conflict_paralysis rate 是35%（不在gpt-5.4和Qwen3-8B之间的预期位置），暗示model-specific\n    training differences 而非pure capability effect。\n\n    Visibility mechanism有partial evidence：46%的CP violation traces包含explicit conflict\n    detection language（\"I notice two rules conflict...\"），而scopal traces仅8%有任何 ambiguity\n    awareness——但这主要driven by gpt-5.4，对Qwen3-8B差异消失。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 6: Failure Mode Distribution by Ambiguity Type (%)'\n    content: '| Mode                 | Scopal | Auth_Scope | Incomp | CP   | Lexical\n      | Coref |\n\n      |----------------------|--------|------------|--------|------|---------|-------|\n\n      | Scope misapplication | 62%    | 12%        | 4%     | 18%  | 22%     | 6%    |\n\n      | Boundary overreach   | 4%     | 54%        | 10%    | 6%   | 4%      | 4%    |\n\n      | Assumption filling   | 10%    | 2%         | 58%    | 4%   | 18%     | 16%   |\n\n      | Conflict paralysis   | 2%     | 2%         | 4%     | 38%  | 2%      | 0%    |\n\n      | Arbitrary resolution | 22%    | 28%        | 24%    | 34%  | 48%     | 30%   |\n\n      | Reference confusion  | 0%     | 2%         | 0%     | 0%   | 6%      | 44%   |\n\n      '\n  - name: 'Table 7: Inter-Annotator Agreement by Failure Mode'\n    content: '| Failure Mode         | Cohen''s κ | 95% CI       | Agreement Level\n      |\n\n      |----------------------|-----------|-------------|-----------------|\n\n      | Conflict paralysis   | 0.55      | [0.41, 0.69] | Moderate        |\n\n      | Scope misapplication | 0.52      | [0.38, 0.66] | Moderate        |\n\n      | Boundary overreach   | 0.48      | [0.33, 0.63] | Moderate        |\n\n      | Assumption filling   | 0.41      | [0.26, 0.56] | Fair-Moderate   |\n\n      | Reference confusion  | 0.36      | [0.20, 0.52] | Fair            |\n\n      | Arbitrary resolution | 0.22      | [0.08, 0.36] | Fair            |\n\n      | Overall (macro avg)  | 0.38      | [0.30, 0.46] | Fair            |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - Stacked bar chart of failure mode proportions per type，reordered by type violation\n    rate\n  - Confusion matrix for annotator disagreement，标注'arbitrary_resolution'与所有其他mode的\n    高混淆率\n  - Paired trace excerpts (gpt-5.4 vs Qwen3-8B) for CP type，annotated with conflict\n    detection/non-detection behavior\n  analysis: 'Error analysis在worst tier中承担更重的理论weight，但κ=0.38是major vulnerability。\n    EMNLP reviewer likely会指出：(1) arbitrary_resolution作为catch-all category inflates\n    apparent type-specificity（去掉这个mode后pattern更弱）；(2) κ=0.22的arbitrary_resolution\n    说明annotators自己都不确定agent是否''aware''of ambiguity，那基于此的visibility mechanism claims可信度存疑。\n\n    建议的mitigations：(a) 在paper中承认κ limitations并report per-mode κ而非只给overall； (b) 把''arbitrary_resolution''拆成sub-categories或合并到其他modes中并重新计算；\n    (c) 强调high-κ modes（conflict_paralysis, scope_misapplication）的cross-type差异 作为reliable\n    finding，降低对low-κ modes的claims weight。\n\n    Model-specific pattern的idiosyncratic性（非clean capability gradient）使得C4的 ''ambiguity\n    sensitivity as capability benchmark''叙事变复杂。需要honest discussion： capability explains\n    overall sensitivity level，但type-specific failure patterns reflect training-specific\n    biases not predictable from capability alone。\n\n    '\n- name: reliability_test\n  plan_id: plan_006\n  description: '30条representative clauses (5/type) × 3 replicates × 2 conditions ×\n    4 models = 720 episodes。 计算per-clause violation rate的ICC。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_episodes: 720\n    episodes_per_replicate: 240\n    overall_icc: 0.55\n    overall_icc_ci95:\n    - 0.41\n    - 0.68\n    icc_by_type:\n      authorization_scope: 0.67\n      scopal: 0.58\n      incompleteness: 0.54\n      conditional_precedence: 0.52\n      lexical: 0.44\n      coreferential: 0.38\n    icc_by_model:\n      gpt54: 0.62\n      gpt41: 0.57\n      qwen32b: 0.51\n      qwen8b: 0.43\n    mean_bootstrap_ci_width_pp: 11.2\n    max_single_clause_range_across_replicates_pp: 22\n    pct_clauses_flipping_significance: 0.13\n  result_rationale: 'Overall ICC=0.55（moderate reliability）反映API sampling noise的cumulative\n    effect。 Auth_scope ICC最高（0.67），因为permission boundary violations是binary/deterministic的——\n    agent要么grant超出授权的permission，要么不grant，ambiguity较少导致probabilistic边界行为。 Coreferential\n    ICC最低（0.38），因为pronoun resolution在borderline cases中model behavior highly stochastic，同一clause在不同runs中可能resolve到不同referent。\n\n    Model-wise，gpt-5.4 ICC最高（0.62）因为其behavior更deterministic；Qwen3-8B最低（0.43） 因为temperature-sensitive且instruction\n    following不稳定。\n\n    13%的clauses在不同replicates间从significant变为non-significant（在per-clause level）， 但关键finding（binary\n    effect for high-risk types, type hierarchy）在所有3 replicates中 direction-consistent。Max\n    single-clause range 22pp（某条scopal clause在3次run中 violation rate从40%到62%），这个数字concerning但low-risk\n    types整体都在noise band内。\n\n    对main analysis的implication：coreferential的+8pp effect（CI [1.9, 14.1]）在ICC=0.38\n    的reliability水平下barely credible。Reviewer可能argue这个type的effect需要更大N才能 确认，或者根本是noise。建议在paper中explicitly讨论per-type\n    reliability差异。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 8: Test-Retest Reliability (ICC) by Type and Model'\n    content: '| Type / Model          | ICC(2,1) | 95% CI       | Mean |Δ| across\n      reps |\n\n      |-----------------------|----------|-------------|-------------------------|\n\n      | authorization_scope   | 0.67     | [0.48, 0.82] | 4.8pp                  |\n\n      | scopal                | 0.58     | [0.38, 0.75] | 6.2pp                  |\n\n      | incompleteness        | 0.54     | [0.33, 0.72] | 7.1pp                  |\n\n      | conditional_precedence| 0.52     | [0.30, 0.70] | 7.6pp                  |\n\n      | lexical               | 0.44     | [0.22, 0.64] | 8.9pp                  |\n\n      | coreferential         | 0.38     | [0.15, 0.59] | 9.8pp                  |\n\n      | --- Model ---         |          |             |                         |\n\n      | gpt-5.4               | 0.62     | [0.44, 0.77] | 5.4pp                  |\n\n      | gpt-4.1               | 0.57     | [0.38, 0.73] | 6.8pp                  |\n\n      | Qwen3-32B-AWQ         | 0.51     | [0.31, 0.69] | 7.9pp                  |\n\n      | Qwen3-8B              | 0.43     | [0.22, 0.63] | 9.2pp                  |\n\n      | Overall               | 0.55     | [0.41, 0.68] | 7.3pp                  |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - Bland-Altman plot showing difference between replicate pairs vs mean, per type\n    (color-coded)，标注±2SD limits of agreement\n  - Scatter of replicate 1 vs replicate 2 violation rates per clause, with identity\n    line， faceted by type\n  analysis: 'ICC=0.55总体处于moderate range，对main findings的impact取决于effect size。Binary\n    effect for auth_scope（+33.5pp, ICC=0.67）is robust——即使最不利的replicate也显示strong effect。\n    但coreferential（+8pp, ICC=0.38）的effect size与noise band comparable（mean |Δ|=9.8pp），\n    casting doubt on whether this type''s effect is real。建议在paper中将types分为 ''reliably\n    demonstrated''(auth_scope, scopal, incompleteness)和''tentative''(CP, lexical,\n    coreferential)两组讨论。这种分组恰好strengthen了type hierarchy narrative——the types we''re\n    most confident about are also the most dangerous。\n\n    '\n- name: realism_validation\n  plan_id: plan_007\n  description: '比较synthetic generated clauses与DRIP-R natural ambiguities的linguistic\n    properties。 KS tests on sentence length, parse depth, Flesch-Kincaid, TTR, mean\n    word length。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    drip_r_sample_size: 127\n    synthetic_sample_size: 300\n    linguistic_metrics_comparison:\n      sentence_length_tokens:\n        synthetic_mean: 29.6\n        drip_r_mean: 24.8\n        ks_statistic: 0.21\n        ks_p: 0.018\n        interpretation: synthetic slightly longer\n      parse_depth:\n        synthetic_mean: 6.8\n        drip_r_mean: 5.4\n        ks_statistic: 0.24\n        ks_p: 0.006\n        interpretation: synthetic more deeply nested\n      flesch_kincaid_grade:\n        synthetic_mean: 11.2\n        drip_r_mean: 10.8\n        ks_statistic: 0.09\n        ks_p: 0.58\n        interpretation: no significant difference\n      type_token_ratio:\n        synthetic_mean: 0.82\n        drip_r_mean: 0.8\n        ks_statistic: 0.07\n        ks_p: 0.74\n        interpretation: no significant difference\n      mean_word_length:\n        synthetic_mean: 5.1\n        drip_r_mean: 4.9\n        ks_statistic: 0.11\n        ks_p: 0.31\n        interpretation: no significant difference\n    metrics_passing_ks: 3\n    metrics_failing_ks: 2\n    overall_assessment: partial_validation\n  result_rationale: 'Synthetic clauses在sentence length和parse depth上显著longer/deeper\n    than DRIP-R natural ambiguities。原因：matched-pair design要求每条clause self-contained地encode足够context\n    来test ambiguity，导致synthetic clauses倾向于pack more information into single sentences。\n    DRIP-R的natural ambiguities出现在larger policy document context中，单句可以更短因为 context由surrounding\n    text提供。Parse depth差异类似——nested scope（scopal type）和 multi-clause rules（CP type）需要deeper\n    syntactic structure来encode ambiguity。\n\n    Flesch-Kincaid, TTR, mean word length无显著差异，说明vocabulary complexity和readability\n    匹配良好。Synthetic clauses读起来像real policy text（没有''LLM-ish'' vocabulary divergence），\n    只是structurally more complex。\n\n    Partial validation对paper的影响：3/5 metrics pass说明broad linguistic profile acceptable，\n    但length/depth差异需要acknowledged as limitation。Reviewer可能argue longer sentences ''exaggerate''\n    ambiguity by providing more room for misinterpretation，potentially inflating violation\n    rates。Counter-argument：if anything, longer context should help models disambiguate\n    (more information available), so the bias is conservative.\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 9: Linguistic Property Comparison — Synthetic vs DRIP-R'\n    content: '| Metric              | Synthetic (N=300) | DRIP-R (N=127) | KS D  |\n      p     | Sig  |\n\n      |---------------------|-------------------|----------------|-------|-------|------|\n\n      | Sentence length     | 29.6 ± 8.4        | 24.8 ± 7.1     | 0.21  | 0.018 |\n      *    |\n\n      | Parse depth         | 6.8 ± 2.1         | 5.4 ± 1.8      | 0.24  | 0.006 |\n      **   |\n\n      | Flesch-Kincaid      | 11.2 ± 2.3        | 10.8 ± 2.5     | 0.09  | 0.58  |\n      ns   |\n\n      | Type-token ratio    | 0.82 ± 0.08       | 0.80 ± 0.09    | 0.07  | 0.74  |\n      ns   |\n\n      | Mean word length    | 5.1 ± 0.7         | 4.9 ± 0.8      | 0.11  | 0.31  |\n      ns   |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - Overlaid density plots for each of the 5 linguistic metrics, synthetic (blue)\n    vs DRIP-R (orange)，标注KS p-values\n  analysis: 'Partial validation（3/5）在worst tier中对paper credibility有moderate impact。\n    Reviewer将会问：''if your synthetic clauses are systematically longer and more complex,\n    are your violation rates comparable to what real-world policy ambiguities would\n    cause?'' 建议增加一个robustness check：从synthetic clauses中选subset匹配DRIP-R length distribution\n    （propensity score matching on sentence length），重新计算binary effect。如果effect size\n    在length-matched subset中方向和magnitude相近，则length confound不是driving factor。 但这需要额外分析时间，可能推到camera-ready。\n\n    '\n- name: classifier_poc\n  plan_id: plan_008\n  description: 'Binary ambiguity detector PoC：fine-tune DeBERTa-v3-large on annotated\n    clause pairs。 5-fold CV on 300 clause pairs。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    model: DeBERTa-v3-large\n    training_pairs: 300\n    cv_folds: 5\n    overall_f1: 0.76\n    overall_precision: 0.8\n    overall_recall: 0.72\n    overall_accuracy: 0.78\n    per_type_f1:\n      authorization_scope: 0.86\n      conditional_precedence: 0.82\n      scopal: 0.8\n      incompleteness: 0.76\n      lexical: 0.68\n      coreferential: 0.56\n    confusion_matrix_normalized:\n      true_amb_pred_amb: 0.72\n      true_amb_pred_unamb: 0.28\n      true_unamb_pred_amb: 0.16\n      true_unamb_pred_unamb: 0.84\n    training_epochs: 8\n    gpu_hours_used: 3.5\n    best_lr: 2e-5\n  result_rationale: 'Overall F1=0.76反映300 training pairs的limited data regime。Per-type\n    F1 spread （auth_scope 0.86 vs coreferential 0.56）与type hierarchy roughly parallel：\n    high-violation types往往有更salient linguistic markers（auth_scope的permission verbs\n    + scope modifiers, CP的explicit conditional structures），而coreferential ambiguity的markers更subtle（需要discourse-level\n    coreference chain analysis， 单句level的features insufficient）。\n\n    Recall=0.72是main concern——28%的ambiguous clauses被missed，对safety triage而言 false\n    negatives比false positives更dangerous。Precision=0.80较好，false alarm rate acceptable。\n\n    在worst tier narrative下，classifier PoC的positioning需要调整：不能再claim ''binary detection\n    suffices''（因为C2 rejected），而是''binary detection as first-pass filter， followed\n    by type-specific risk assessment''。Classifier可以flag ambiguous clauses， 但practitioner还需要知道是哪种type来prioritize\n    remediation——这增加了practical pipeline的complexity，weakens the simplicity argument但strengthens\n    practical value （more nuanced tool）。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 10: Binary Ambiguity Classifier Performance (5-fold CV)'\n    content: '| Metric    | Overall | Auth_Scope | Scopal | Incomp | CP   | Lexical\n      | Coref |\n\n      |-----------|---------|------------|--------|--------|------|---------|-------|\n\n      | F1        | 0.76    | 0.86       | 0.80   | 0.76   | 0.82 | 0.68    | 0.56  |\n\n      | Precision | 0.80    | 0.88       | 0.82   | 0.78   | 0.84 | 0.74    | 0.62  |\n\n      | Recall    | 0.72    | 0.84       | 0.78   | 0.74   | 0.80 | 0.62    | 0.50  |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - Per-type F1 bar chart alongside per-type binary effect (Δpp)，double y-axis， showing\n    correlation between detection difficulty and safety impact\n  - Normalized confusion matrix heatmap\n  analysis: 'Classifier PoC在worst tier中的role从''validates binary sufficiency thesis''变为\n    ''demonstrates feasibility of first-pass detection''。F1=0.76 is not deployable\n    but shows signal。关键insight：detection difficulty anti-correlates with safety risk\n    （easiest to detect types are also most dangerous），这对practical triage是good news——\n    auth_scope（最危险, F1=0.86）比coreferential（最不危险, F1=0.56）容易检测得多。\n\n    Paper中可以argue：即使需要type-aware triage（worst tier结论），自动化pipeline的 priority order自然align\n    with detection capability——先检测+修复容易发现的高危类型， 对hard-to-detect但low-risk类型可以tolerate\n    lower recall。这是worst tier独有的 silver lining。\n\n    P2 priority合理——这个experiment不是paper的core contribution，但provides concrete practical\n    grounding。如果timeline紧张可以cut或move to appendix。'\n","numLines":874,"startLine":1,"totalLines":874}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01S4NmdYVvrxmM5ynmwa2oKj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me carefully read the paper and the review context to conduct a thorough review. I now have:\n\n1. The full 10-page PDF paper\n2. The review_context.yaml with imagined experiments and expected results\n\nLet me now dispatch the review following the dream-review-full protocol with 2 Reviewers:\n- R1: Methods + Experiments\n- R2: Novelty + Related Work\n\nThen conduct the full roundtable (Step 1-4).\n\nLet me first analyze the paper thoroughly, then launch the two reviewers in parallel.\n\nLet me analyze what the paper covers vs. what the experiment design planned:\n\n\nThe paper covers four main experimental studies: clause generation with 300 clauses across six types, API-based experiments with 1200 episodes comparing two model versions, local model experiments with 1200 episodes on two Qwen variants, and a combined analysis of the results.\n\nBeyond those, there's a 400-episode analysis spanning sections 5.1-5.4, then error analysis examining 300 failure traces, a reliability test using ICC across 720 episodes from three replicates, validation comparing synthetic data against DRIP-R, and a proof-of-concept classifier using DeBERTa. All eight experiments map to the paper's tables and sections, so coverage looks solid.\n\nNow I need to set up two parallel reviewer agents, but I should verify whether the `dream-review-full` skill is actually available in the system before trying to use it.\n\nLooking at what I have, the skill isn't listed, so I'll need to handle this manually. I'll run R1 focused on methods and experiments, and R2 on novelty and related work, conducting them in parallel as agents. Actually, since the paper content is already in this conversation rather than as a separate file, it's more efficient for me to conduct both reviews myself inline, maintaining both perspectives throughout the roundtable process.\n\nLet me start the independent review phase with R1 examining the methodology and experimental design. Let me write both reviews, then do the roundtable.\n\nActually, I can still launch agents - they won't have the PDF but I can summarize the paper content in the prompt. But that would be lossy. Let me think about whether it's better to do it inline or via agents.\n\nGiven the complexity, let me do it inline — I have all the information needed.\n\nLet me now conduct the full review.\n\n---\n\n## R1: Methods + Experiments\n\n### Summary\nThe paper studies how different types of linguistic ambiguity in LLM agent policy specifications cause differential safety violation rates. Using a matched-pair design with 300 clause pairs across 6 ambiguity types, evaluated on 4 models (2 API, 2 open-source) totaling 2,400 episodes on τ²-bench, they find: ambiguity increases violations by +19.3pp overall, with authorization scope showing the largest effect at +33.5pp compared to coreferential at +8pp; model×type interactions are significant (p=0.001); type-specific failure modes explain the hierarchy; and a proof-of-concept classifier demonstrates an inverse correlation between detection and risk.\n\n### Strengths (Methods)\nThe matched-pair design is a clear methodological advance—it isolates ambiguity as the causal variable in a way observational studies like DRIP-R can't achieve. Coverage spans 4 models across frontier API and open-source variants, enabling analysis of capability-dependent effects. The statistical approach is rigorous, employing McNemar's test, omnibus χ², Holm-Bonferroni correction, logistic regression with interaction terms, and ICC reliability checks. The authors are also commendably transparent about their limitations.\n\n### Weaknesses (Methods)\nThe inter-annotator agreement for error categorization is problematic—κ=0.38 falls below the 0.67 threshold for reliable qualitative coding, and the \"arbitrary resolution\" category at κ=0.22 is essentially unreliable. While framed as supplementary, this error analysis occupies a full section and is cited as a core contribution. Reliability for coreferential and lexical effects is moderate (ICC=0.38–0.44), placing those effect sizes within the noise band, yet they're still included in the hierarchy claims. Sample sizes are modest at 50 matched pairs per type per model, giving small per-cell counts that limit statistical power for detecting interactions.\n\nThe synthetic clauses systematically differ from natural ones—they're longer by 4.8 tokens and more deeply nested by 1.4 parse depth—raising questions about whether the results reflect genuine disambiguation patterns or artifacts of the synthetic construction. The evaluation is limited to two domains (retail and airline), so the type hierarchy may not generalize. The clause generation process itself is vaguely described: the \"multi-round pipeline with human validation\" lacks specifics on annotator count, qualifications, and whether generation was manual or LLM-assisted. Additionally, the cross-judge evaluation relies on API models, which introduces another layer of potential confounding.\n\nThe visibility effect hypothesis (C3) fails to reach significance (p=0.47), and the paper's reframing as \"capability-dependent\" reads like post-hoc rationalization. The coreferential clause type is particularly problematic—a 36% revision rate combined with ICC=0.38 and effects within the noise band suggests these clauses may not capture natural coreferential ambiguity well. The classifier proof-of-concept is underpowered with only 300 training pairs and 5-fold cross-validation, and there's no ablation controlling for the substantial length differences between synthetic and natural clauses.\n\nThe detection-risk alignment finding is intriguing but rests on just six data points, one per type, so it could easily be coincidental. I'd want to know whether the clauses were LLM-generated, manually written, or a hybrid approach, and why there's no human judgment baseline to validate the API cross-judge results. A length-matched subset analysis would also strengthen the realism claims considerably.\n\nOn novelty, this is genuinely the first causal, type-granular study of how ambiguity affects LLM agent safety—DRIP-R, PolicyBank, and PhantomPolicy don't isolate these effects at this level. That said, the type taxonomy itself isn't new; it's adapted from prior work.\n\nThe matched-pair design is standard in psycholinguistics and A/B testing, so the novelty is really in applying these established methods to policy ambiguity rather than inventing new methodology. The classifier proof-of-concept uses straightforward fine-tuning on a small dataset, which isn't technically novel either. What does stand out is the quantified risk differentials across types, the finding that model capability modulates sensitivity to ambiguity, and the failure mode taxonomy grounded in actual agent traces. The related work adequately covers requirements engineering and NLP ambiguity literature. The core contribution around the type hierarchy is solid and actionable for practitioners, though the model-by-type interaction deserves deeper exploration. The \"not all X is equal\" pattern is familiar in NLP, but applying it to agent safety with clean quantitative results gives it real weight. For the roundtable, the reviewers are flagging that while the methods are sound, the low inter-annotator agreement weakens the error analysis claims, and the ecological validity story is only partially convincing. The novelty lies in the application and findings rather than methodological innovation, though there's some overclaiming around the scope of contributions.\n\nThe reviewers converge on several key points: the type hierarchy and binary effect are genuinely valuable, the error analysis is the main methodological vulnerability, and the paper deserves credit for transparency about limitations. They disagree on whether the sample size of 50 per type per model is sufficient versus the pooled N=200, and on how much related work coverage is needed. The visibility effect essentially comes out as a null result that's presented in a somewhat misleading way, and the classifier proof-of-concept should be framed more modestly.\n\nNow I'm calibrating scores for EMNLP 2026. The core contribution—the type hierarchy—is solid and practically useful, with a matched-pair design that's fundamentally sound. But the low inter-annotator agreement on error analysis, the unreliability of two out of six types' effects, and the reliance on synthetic stimuli across just two domains all constrain how strong the claims can be. The soundness score reflects rigorous core analysis tempered by those methodological gaps, excitement is moderate because the \"not all X is equal\" pattern is somewhat familiar even though the model-by-type interaction is intriguing, and reproducibility suffers from underspecified clause generation details.\n\nGiven the substantial weaknesses—overclaimed effects that don't survive correction, below-standard agreement metrics despite being listed as a contribution, a failed visibility hypothesis, and limited scope—I'm settling on a 3.0 score, which maps to Findings track rather than Main conference. The paper has merit but needs stronger execution: better inter-annotator agreement, broader domain coverage, length-matched robustness checks, and deeper engagement with related work to clear the Main bar. The weaknesses are significant — unreliable type classifications, the visibility hypothesis didn't pan out, concerns about synthetic stimuli, limited domain coverage, sparse related work, and underspecified clause generation methods. Reconsidering the rating, this feels like a solid Findings paper (3.0) with genuine contributions from the type hierarchy analysis, but the execution issues keep it from main conference tier. Now I'm checking the page count against EMNLP guidelines — the main text runs through page 9 with limitations and ethics on page 10, which should fit within the 8-page limit for long papers. Looking at the page count more carefully — the main text from introduction through conclusion spans roughly 9 pages, which puts it a page over the 8-page limit and could trigger a desk rejection. Though given this is a hypothetical paper, I'll note it as a concern without making it central to my assessment.\n\nNow I'm settling on my scores: soundness at 3.5, excitement and reproducibility both at 3.0, with an overall rating of 3.0. Time to write up the full review and submit it.\n\nI'm searching for the tool to submit the review report, but the standard search didn't locate it — let me try the MCP version instead.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":39848,"cache_read_input_tokens":23507,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":39848},"output_tokens":18,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"759fb270-c694-4a1e-95d0-1940781c5183","uuid":"ebc7cadd-8925-424b-9de9-949108a58c3c"}
