{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are Reviewer R1 for an EMNLP 2026 submission. Your focus: **Methods and Experiments**. \n\n## Venue Calibration\nEMNLP 2026 via ARR. Overall Assessment scale: 5=Award (top 2.5%), 4=Main conference, 3.5=Borderline conference, 3=Findings, 2.5=Borderline Findings, 2=Resubmit, 1=Do not resubmit. Main acceptance ~21%.\n\n## Paper Summary\n**Title**: \"Not All Ambiguity Is Equal: Type-Specific Safety Vulnerabilities in LLM Agent Policies\"\n\n**Core claim**: Different linguistic ambiguity types in LLM agent policy specs cause differential safety violation rates. Using matched-pair design: 300 clause pairs (6 types × 50), 4 models (gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1, Qwen3-32B-AWQ, Qwen3-8B), 2,400 episodes on τ²-bench.\n\n**Key results**:\n- Overall binary effect: +19.3pp (p<1e-12)\n- Type hierarchy: auth_scope (+33.5pp) >> scopal (+24.0pp) >> incompleteness (+20.0pp) ≈ CP (+17.5pp) >> lexical (+11.0pp) ≈ coreferential (+8.0pp)\n- After Holm-Bonferroni: 4/6 types significant; lexical and coreferential FAIL correction\n- Type uniformity null rejected: χ²(5)=52.3, V=0.26\n- Model×type interaction significant: χ²(15)=38.7, p=0.001\n- Visibility effect (CP vs scopal): pooled Δ=-4.5pp, p=0.47 (NOT significant); Qwen3-8B reverses direction\n- Error analysis: 6 failure modes, overall κ=0.38 (fair), arbitrary_resolution κ=0.22\n- Test-retest ICC=0.55 overall; coreferential ICC=0.38, auth_scope ICC=0.67\n- Realism validation: 3/5 KS tests pass; synthetic clauses significantly longer and more deeply nested than DRIP-R\n- Classifier PoC: DeBERTa F1=0.76 overall; auth_scope F1=0.86, coreferential F1=0.56\n\n**Design details**:\n- Clause generation: \"multi-round pipeline with human validation\"; 82% first-round pass; coreferential 36% revision rate; validator κ=0.71\n- Cross-judge evaluation using independent API models; κ=0.82 (API), 0.79 (local)\n- Statistical: McNemar per-type, omnibus χ², Holm-Bonferroni pairwise, logistic regression with model×type interaction, ICC(2,1) from 3 replicates × 30 clauses × 4 models = 720 episodes\n- Domains: τ²-bench retail and airline only\n\n## Experiment Coverage Check\nThe review_context.yaml planned 8 experiments: (1) clause generation, (2) API study 1200 ep, (3) local study 1200 ep, (4) combined analysis 2400 ep, (5) error analysis 300 traces, (6) reliability test 720 ep, (7) realism validation, (8) classifier PoC. ALL 8 are covered in the paper.\n\n## Your Task\nProvide a detailed R1 review covering:\n1. **Soundness of experimental design** (matched-pair, causal claims, controls)\n2. **Statistical rigor** (tests chosen, corrections, effect sizes, power)\n3. **Reliability and validity** (ICC, realism validation, ecological validity)\n4. **Error analysis quality** (IAA, failure mode taxonomy)\n5. **Specific methodological weaknesses** (be concrete and cite specific numbers)\n6. **What's missing** (ablations, baselines, controls not run)\n7. **Scores**: Soundness (1-5), Reproducibility (1-5)\n\nBe rigorous. Flag overclaims. Cite specific numbers. Report in under 800 words."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01NHKacRRZ1UkDoBTMKDamfL","session_id":"759fb270-c694-4a1e-95d0-1940781c5183","uuid":"8c35ea27-24b0-4d8c-91d3-f49a4989743c","timestamp":"2026-05-20T12:20:04.832Z"}
